window.DOCS["6ae094e458b9a83bc4d4c2ff"]={"id":"6ae094e458b9a83bc4d4c2ff","summary":{"title_zh":"議程項目 8 (b) 資源動員與財務機制：財務機制非正式文本（第 3 版）","what":"這是第一工作小組的非正式文本（第 3 版），內容涉及全球環境基金（GEF）第九次增資期間（2026 年 7 月至 2030 年 6 月）的捐款承諾、資源分配、成效要求，以及對第十次增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）所需資金的評估安排。","points":["[尚未達成共識] 敦促（或請求）已開發國家締約方，並邀請其他承擔已開發國家義務的締約方與其他國家，為全球環境基金第九次增資捐款，以支持綱要的全面執行，並依公約第 20 條辦理。","歡迎全球環境基金將第九次增資資源的 35% 分配給生物多樣性重點領域，並以至少 70% 的資金投入生物多樣性為目標。","請求全球環境基金加快強化成效，包括改善環境公約之間的協同、促進私部門投資，並降低交易成本、簡化申請程序、加快撥款，特別是支持低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家。","請求全球環境基金深化對原住民族與地方社區的支持，包括為其在全組合中佔 20% 的目標制定指引（直接取得資金模式與原住民族、女性及青年參與的措辭尚未達成共識）。","請求執行秘書準備報告，評估開發中國家締約方在第十次增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）履行公約所需的資金（附件二的評估職權範圍尚未達成共識）。"],"open":["第 1–2 段：對第九次增資承諾（約 39 億美元）的用語（歡迎、確認或感謝），以及「僅 50% 已開發國家締約方出資」之措辭（整段方括號）（尚未達成共識）。","第 3 段：第九次增資較第八次減少 27%，是否應「深表關切」，或改為「整體資源仍不足以因應綱要與公約的需求」（尚未達成共識）。","第 4 段：請求已開發國家繳款時，動詞應為「敦促」還是「請求」（尚未達成共識）。","第 11 段與第 12(g) 段：全球環境基金治理準則是否應納入原住民族、女性與青年的參與機制（尚未達成共識）。","第 25 段：是否「要求」為生物安全專案保留特定資源，或僅「鼓勵」開發中國家締約方向全球環境基金提出生物安全專案（尚未達成共識）。","第 34 段、第 39(a) 段、附件二與附件三：第十次增資的完整評估職權範圍、第七次四年期財務機制審查，以及是否比較全球環境基金與綠色氣候基金等多邊機制（尚未達成共識）。"]},"summaryReviewed":true,"pages":[{"p":"p001","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae094e458b9a83bc4d4c2ff/p001.md","en":"Agenda item 8 (b)\nResource mobilization and financial\nmechanism: financial mechanism\nWorking Group I\n\n       Financial mechanism\n       Non-paper\n\n               The Conference of the Parties,\n              Recalling its decisions 15/15 of 19 December 2022 and 16/33 of 27 February 2025 pertaining\n       to the assessment of funding needed by all eligible developing country Parties, in particular the least\n       developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition for\n       the implementation of the Convention on Biological Diversity 1 and its Protocols for the ninth\n       replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (July 2026–June 2030),\n              Recalling also the four-year outcome-oriented framework of biodiversity programme\n       priorities of the Convention and its Protocols for the ninth replenishment period of the Global\n       Environment Facility Trust Fund contained in annex I to decision 16/33,\n              Recognizing that the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework2 is relevant to all\n       biodiversity-related conventions and other multilateral environmental agreements and the mandate\n       of the Global Environment Facility,\n             [1. [Welcomes][Acknowledges][Notes with appreciation] the pledges made as at 30 May\n       2026 for the ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund by participant\n       countries, namely, Australia, Austria, Belgium, Brazil, Canada, China, Côte d’Ivoire, France,\n       Germany, India, Ireland, Italy, Japan, Luxembourg, Mexico, Netherlands (Kingdom of the), New\n       Zealand, Norway, Slovenia, South Africa, Switzerland and Uzbekistan, which amounted to\n       approximately 3.9 billion United States dollars, using the agreed reference exchange rates for the\n       replenishment period;3]\n             [2. Notes with concern that the amount of 3.9 billion dollars is contributed by only 50 per\n       cent of developed country Parties, and appreciates the contributions of developing country Parties,\n       namely, Brazil, China, Côte d’Ivoire, India, Mexico, South Africa and Uzbekistan;4]\n              [3. [Notes with deep concern] that [the negotiations for the ninth replenishment of the\n       Global Environment Facility Trust Fund concluded with a reduction of 27 per cent compared with\n       the eighth replenishment period and that such a reduction comes at a time when Parties are expected\n       to accelerate the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework][the\n       overall level of resources remains insufficient in the light of the scale of needs to implement the\n       Convention on Biological Diversity and its Protocols and the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity\n       Framework, in particular Target 19 (a);]]5\n\n\n\n1 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.\n2 Decision 15/4, annex.\n3 To be updated in October 2026.\n4 To be updated in October 2026.\n5 Operative paragraphs 1 to 3 were considered at the seventh meeting of the Subsidiary Body on Implementation (see\n\nrecommendation 7/3). Recommendation 6/2, adopted at its sixth meeting, also contained a paragraph on the topic of the ninth\nreplenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (para. 6), but that paragraph was not discussed at that\nmeeting. It is the understanding of the Secretariat that paragraphs 1 to 3 above reflect the discussions of the Subsidiary Body on\nthe subject and therefore supersede the not-negotiated paragraph 6 in recommendation 6/2. As a result, that paragraph has not\nbeen included in the present draft decision. For reference, it read as follows: “[Reiterates its appreciation to developed country\nParties, other Parties that voluntarily assume the obligations of developed country Parties and other donors that contributed\nactively to the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund and the ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund\nin support of eligible developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States,\n[the most environmentally vulnerable country Parties,] and Parties with economies in transition;]”.","blocks":[{"md":"議程項目 8 (b)\n資源動員與財務機制：財務機制\n第一工作小組","html":"<p>議程項目 8 (b)<br />\n資源動員與財務機制：財務機制<br />\n第一工作小組</p>"},{"md":"財務機制\n非正式文件（Non-paper）","html":"<p>財務機制<br />\n非正式文件（Non-paper）</p>"},{"md":"締約方大會，","html":"<p>締約方大會，</p>"},{"md":"**回顧**其 2022 年 12 月 19 日之決議 15/15 以及 2025 年 2 月 27 日之決議 16/33，關於評估所有符合條件之開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中締約方，為執行《生物多樣性公約》¹ 及其議定書，於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間（2026 年 7 月至 2030 年 6 月）所需之資金；","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong>其 2022 年 12 月 19 日之決議 15/15 以及 2025 年 2 月 27 日之決議 16/33，關於評估所有符合條件之開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中締約方，為執行《生物多樣性公約》¹ 及其議定書，於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間（2026 年 7 月至 2030 年 6 月）所需之資金；</p>"},{"md":"**亦回顧**決議 16/33 附件一所載，關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間，該公約及其議定書之生物多樣性計畫優先事項之四年期成果導向框架；","html":"<p><strong>亦回顧</strong>決議 16/33 附件一所載，關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間，該公約及其議定書之生物多樣性計畫優先事項之四年期成果導向框架；</p>"},{"md":"**認識到**《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》² 與所有生物多樣性相關公約及其他多邊環境協議，以及全球環境基金之職權相關；","html":"<p><strong>認識到</strong>《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》² 與所有生物多樣性相關公約及其他多邊環境協議，以及全球環境基金之職權相關；</p>"},{"md":"[1. [歡迎][承認][表示感謝地注意到] 截至 2026 年 5 月 30 日止，參與國為全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資所做出之承諾，即：澳洲、奧地利、比利時、巴西、加拿大、中國、象牙海岸、法國、德國、印度、愛爾蘭、義大利、日本、盧森堡、墨西哥、荷蘭（王國）、紐西蘭、挪威、斯洛維尼亞、南非、瑞士及烏茲別克，其金額依增資期間約定之參考匯率計算，總計約 39 億美元；³]","html":"<p>[1. [歡迎][承認][表示感謝地注意到] 截至 2026 年 5 月 30 日止，參與國為全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資所做出之承諾，即：澳洲、奧地利、比利時、巴西、加拿大、中國、象牙海岸、法國、德國、印度、愛爾蘭、義大利、日本、盧森堡、墨西哥、荷蘭（王國）、紐西蘭、挪威、斯洛維尼亞、南非、瑞士及烏茲別克，其金額依增資期間約定之參考匯率計算，總計約 39 億美元；³]</p>"},{"md":"[2. **憂心地注意到** 39 億美元之金額僅由 50% 的已開發國家締約方所貢獻，並**歡迎**開發中國家締約方之貢獻，即：巴西、中國、象牙海岸、印度、墨西哥、南非及烏茲別克；⁴]","html":"<p>[2. <strong>憂心地注意到</strong> 39 億美元之金額僅由 50% 的已開發國家締約方所貢獻，並<strong>歡迎</strong>開發中國家締約方之貢獻，即：巴西、中國、象牙海岸、印度、墨西哥、南非及烏茲別克；⁴]</p>"},{"md":"[3. [**深切憂心地注意到**] [全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資之談判結果，與第八期增資期間相比減少了 27%，且此類減少發生在締約方預期應加速執行《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之時期][鑑於執行《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》（特別是目標 19 (a)）之需求規模，整體資源水準仍然不足；]]⁵","html":"<p>[3. [<strong>深切憂心地注意到</strong>] [全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資之談判結果，與第八期增資期間相比減少了 27%，且此類減少發生在締約方預期應加速執行《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之時期][鑑於執行《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》（特別是目標 19 (a)）之需求規模，整體資源水準仍然不足；]]⁵</p>"},{"md":"---\n¹ 聯合國，《條約集》，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。\n² 決議 15/4，附件。\n³ 將於 2026 年 10 月更新。\n⁴ 將於 2026 年 10 月更新。\n⁵ 執行附屬機構第七次會議已審議決議草案第 1 至 3 段（參見建議 7/3）。其第六次會議所通過之建議 6/2 亦包含一段關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資主題之段落（第 6 段），但該段落未在該次會議中進行討論。秘書處之理解為，上述第 1 至 3 段反映了附屬機構就該主題之討論，因此取代建議 6/2 中尚未經談判之第 6 段。因此，該段落未包含在本決議草案中。供參考，其原文如下：「[重申對已開發國家締約方、自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之其他締約方，以及為支持符合條件之開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家、[環境最脆弱之締約方] 以及經濟轉型中締約方）而對全球生物多樣性綱要基金及全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資做出積極貢獻之其他捐助者，表示感謝；]」。","html":"<hr />\n<p>¹ 聯合國，《條約集》，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n² 決議 15/4，附件。<br />\n³ 將於 2026 年 10 月更新。<br />\n⁴ 將於 2026 年 10 月更新。<br />\n⁵ 執行附屬機構第七次會議已審議決議草案第 1 至 3 段（參見建議 7/3）。其第六次會議所通過之建議 6/2 亦包含一段關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資主題之段落（第 6 段），但該段落未在該次會議中進行討論。秘書處之理解為，上述第 1 至 3 段反映了附屬機構就該主題之討論，因此取代建議 6/2 中尚未經談判之第 6 段。因此，該段落未包含在本決議草案中。供參考，其原文如下：「[重申對已開發國家締約方、自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之其他締約方，以及為支持符合條件之開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家、[環境最脆弱之締約方] 以及經濟轉型中締約方）而對全球生物多樣性綱要基金及全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資做出積極貢獻之其他捐助者，表示感謝；]」。</p>"}]},{"p":"p002","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae094e458b9a83bc4d4c2ff/p002.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 3 – 27 October 2026\n\n              4.    [Urges][Requests] developed country Parties, and invites other Parties that voluntarily\n        assume the obligations of developed country Parties and other countries, to make contributions for\n        the ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund in support of the full\n        implementation of the Framework and in accordance with the provisions of Article 20 of the\n        Convention;\n              5.    Welcomes the report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility for the\n        seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;6\n               6.    Also welcomes the improved disaggregation of co-financing by source in the report of\n        the Council of the Global Environment Facility and encourages the Facility to continue to enhance\n        the transparency and granularity of future reporting on the various sources of co-financing;\n              7.     Notes with appreciation that the programming directions for the ninth replenishment\n        period have been designed to deliver on all elements of the four-year outcome-oriented framework\n        of biodiversity programme priorities of the Convention and its Protocols for the ninth replenishment\n        period adopted by the Conference of the Parties at its sixteenth meeting,7 reflecting the effective\n        response to the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties;\n              8.     Welcomes the allocation of 35 per cent of the ninth replenishment resources to the\n        biodiversity focal area, which is the largest focal area, and the aim of committing at least 70 per cent\n        of funding to biodiversity over that period, according to the Rio marker methodology of the\n        Development Assistance Committee of the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and\n        Development;\n               9.     Also welcomes the inclusion in the programming directions and policy\n        recommendations of the Global Environment Facility for the ninth replenishment period of the\n        indigenous people and local community conservation initiative, 8 an aspirational target of\n        programming 20 per cent of resources to support indigenous peoples and local communities and\n        strengthened support to least developed countries and small island developing States, with an\n        aspirational benchmark of 35 per cent for those countries, as well as the introduction of the\n        aspirational target of programming 25 per cent to mobilize private capital;\n               10. Further welcomes the establishment of the Ad Hoc Governance Working Group of the\n        Council of the Global Environment Facility under the ninth replenishment of the Facility, in response\n        to decision 16/33;\n               [11. Requests the Council of the Global Environment Facility to take into account the criteria\n        [set out in paragraph 21 of decision 16/34 of 27 February 2025] [and decision 17/--], ensuring a\n        democratic and transparent system of governance that is fair, equitable, inclusive, efficient and\n        representative[, while facilitating the full and effective participation of indigenous people and local\n        communities, women and youth];]\n               12. Requests the Global Environment Facility to accelerate efforts to further strengthen its\n        effectiveness, including by:\n              (a) Improving integration pathways, approaches and integrated programmes that deliver\n        system-wide environmental benefits to improve synergies among environmental conventions, while\n        ensuring that such programmes take into account their respective mandates, remain country-driven,\n        responsive to national circumstances and priorities, and implemented through meaningful\n        engagement with national executing agencies from recipient countries;\n              (b) Enabling and facilitating private sector financing aligned with the objectives of the\n        Convention through its blended finance programme funding window and the provision of predictable\n        support to eligible Parties, with a view to developing projects and programmes that enable greater\n\n6 CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1.\n7 Decision 16/33, annex I.\n8 Building on previous iterations of the Inclusive Conservation Initiative at an expanded level of 100 million dollars,\n\n\n\n2/14","blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日</p>"},{"md":"4.\n[敦促][請求] 已開發國家締約方，並邀請其他自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之國家，為全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資提供貢獻，以支持綱要之全面實施，並符合公約第二十條之規定；","html":"<p>4.<br />\n[敦促][請求] 已開發國家締約方，並邀請其他自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之國家，為全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資提供貢獻，以支持綱要之全面實施，並符合公約第二十條之規定；</p>"},{"md":"5.\n**歡迎**全球環境基金理事會提交予第十七次締約方大會之報告；⁶","html":"<p>5.<br />\n<strong>歡迎</strong>全球環境基金理事會提交予第十七次締約方大會之報告；⁶</p>"},{"md":"6.\n亦**歡迎**全球環境基金理事會報告中，針對共同融資來源所進行之改進後的分類統計，並**鼓勵**基金持續提升未來關於各類共同融資來源報告之透明度與細粒度；","html":"<p>6.<br />\n亦<strong>歡迎</strong>全球環境基金理事會報告中，針對共同融資來源所進行之改進後的分類統計，並<strong>鼓勵</strong>基金持續提升未來關於各類共同融資來源報告之透明度與細粒度；</p>"},{"md":"7.\n**注意到**第九次增資期間之規劃方向，旨在落實締約方大會於第十六次會議所通過之公約及其議定書四年期、以成果為導向之生物多樣性計畫優先事項之所有要素，⁷，反映了對締約方所提供之指引之有效回應，並對此表示讚賞；","html":"<p>7.<br />\n<strong>注意到</strong>第九次增資期間之規劃方向，旨在落實締約方大會於第十六次會議所通過之公約及其議定書四年期、以成果為導向之生物多樣性計畫優先事項之所有要素，⁷，反映了對締約方所提供之指引之有效回應，並對此表示讚賞；</p>"},{"md":"8.\n**歡迎**將第九次增資資源之 35% 分配至生物多樣性重點領域（此為最大之重點領域），且根據經濟合作暨發展組織開發援助委員會之里約標記法（Rio marker methodology），其目標為在該期間內將至少 70% 的資金投入於生物多樣性；","html":"<p>8.<br />\n<strong>歡迎</strong>將第九次增資資源之 35% 分配至生物多樣性重點領域（此為最大之重點領域），且根據經濟合作暨發展組織開發援助委員會之里約標記法（Rio marker methodology），其目標為在該期間內將至少 70% 的資金投入於生物多樣性；</p>"},{"md":"9.\n亦**歡迎**在全球環境基金第九次增資期間之規劃方向與政策建議中，納入原住民族與地方社區保育倡議，⁸，其目標為規劃 20% 之資源以支持原住民族與地方社區，並強化對低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家的支持（對該等國家之目標基準為 35%），以及引入規劃 25% 之資源以動員私人資本之目標性目標；","html":"<p>9.<br />\n亦<strong>歡迎</strong>在全球環境基金第九次增資期間之規劃方向與政策建議中，納入原住民族與地方社區保育倡議，⁸，其目標為規劃 20% 之資源以支持原住民族與地方社區，並強化對低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家的支持（對該等國家之目標基準為 35%），以及引入規劃 25% 之資源以動員私人資本之目標性目標；</p>"},{"md":"10. 進一步**歡迎**根據決議 16/33，在全球環境基金第九次增資下，成立全球環境基金理事會特設治理工作小組；","html":"<p>10. 進一步<strong>歡迎</strong>根據決議 16/33，在全球環境基金第九次增資下，成立全球環境基金理事會特設治理工作小組；</p>"},{"md":"[11. **請求**全球環境基金理事會考慮[於 2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/34 第 21 段所列之][及決議 17/--]之標準，確保建立一個公平、公正、包容、高效且具代表性的民主且透明之治理系統[, 並促進原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年之全面且有效參與];]","html":"<p>[11. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金理事會考慮[於 2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/34 第 21 段所列之][及決議 17/--]之標準，確保建立一個公平、公正、包容、高效且具代表性的民主且透明之治理系統[, 並促進原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年之全面且有效參與];]</p>"},{"md":"12. **請求**全球環境基金加速其進一步強化效能之努力，包括透過以下方式：\n(a) 改進整合路徑、方法與整合計畫，以提供全系統之環境效益，從而增進環境公約間之綜效，同時確保此類計畫考量其各自之職權，保持由國家主導，並回應國家情況與優先事項，且透過與受援國國家執行機構之實質參與來實施；\n(b) 透過其混合金融計畫之資助窗口，並向符合條件之締約方提供可預測之支持，使符合公約目標之私部門融資得以實現並獲得促進，其目的在於開發能實現更大規模之專案與計畫","html":"<p>12. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金加速其進一步強化效能之努力，包括透過以下方式：<br />\n(a) 改進整合路徑、方法與整合計畫，以提供全系統之環境效益，從而增進環境公約間之綜效，同時確保此類計畫考量其各自之職權，保持由國家主導，並回應國家情況與優先事項，且透過與受援國國家執行機構之實質參與來實施；<br />\n(b) 透過其混合金融計畫之資助窗口，並向符合條件之締約方提供可預測之支持，使符合公約目標之私部門融資得以實現並獲得促進，其目的在於開發能實現更大規模之專案與計畫</p>"},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />"},{"md":"⁶ CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1。\n⁷ 決議 16/33，附件 I。\n⁸ 在先前規模擴大至 1 億美元之包容性保育倡議基礎上，","html":"<p>⁶ CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1。<br />\n⁷ 決議 16/33，附件 I。<br />\n⁸ 在先前規模擴大至 1 億美元之包容性保育倡議基礎上，</p>"}]},{"p":"p003","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae094e458b9a83bc4d4c2ff/p003.md","en":"                                                                   Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 3 – 27 October 2026\n\n       private sector investment and financial flows, including through long-term enabling policy\n       frameworks, incentives, regulations, blended finance tools and the development of financially viable,\n       investment-ready biodiversity finance projects and pipelines, while recognizing that such\n       investments complement public finance;\n             (c) Promoting whole-of-society and whole-of-government approaches, as appropriate and\n       in accordance with national circumstances, to strengthen programme and project ownership at the\n       national level and the alignment of biodiversity actions with nationally identified priorities, national\n       biodiversity strategies and action plans, national development priorities, and policy coherence;\n              (d) Continuing to improve its system of resource allocation[9] [[, including by continuing\n       to maximize the generation of global environmental benefits and recognizing the role of indigenous\n       peoples and local communities in achieving them, and to improve the allocation performance of its\n       implementing entities] [by enhancing transparency, equity, predictability and responsiveness to the\n       [relevant][specific] needs and priorities of developing country Parties, including small island\n       developing States and least developed countries]];\n              (e) Sustaining enhanced support for all eligible Parties, in particular least developed\n       countries, small island developing States [and the most environmentally vulnerable countries], by\n       reducing transaction costs, simplifying access procedures across existing Global Environment\n       Facility focal areas and financing windows[, including through direct access modalities via national\n       implementing agencies,] and improving the timeliness and predictability of financial support,\n       measured by the date of first disbursement to the recipient country;\n              (f)   Deepening accessible support for indigenous peoples and local communities, in line\n       with element 8 of the programme of work on Article 8(j) and other provisions of the Convention\n       related to indigenous peoples and local communities to 203010 (access, including direct access, to\n       funding for indigenous peoples and local communities for the conservation, restoration and\n       sustainable use of biodiversity), including by developing guidance on the 20 per cent portfolio-wide\n       target for indigenous peoples and local communities, which includes the [dedicated][[direct]\n       access][11] modalities;\n              [(g) Strengthening the full, equitable, inclusive, effective and gender-responsive\n       participation of indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth[, including in decision-\n       making,] in accordance with the national legislation of concerned Parties;]\n              (h) Continuing to promote country-driven national initiatives and regionally coordinated\n       regional and multi-country initiatives[, including transboundary initiatives, with effective\n       participation [and formal approval] [of national focal points for the Convention and relevant national\n       authorities] [and formal approval of operational focal points for the Global Environment Facility]];\n             (i)    Ensuring that Global Environment Facility support for the implementation of the\n       Convention[, including support [through direct access [ 12 ]] for the implementation, monitoring,\n       update and review of national biodiversity strategies and action plans,] is country-led and aligned\n       with [national biodiversity strategies and action plans and] the targets of the Framework;\n\n\n[9 Ensuring that any performance-based element of the allocation formula, including any measure of past disbursement, does not\ndisadvantage Parties the disbursement rates of which reflect the capacity constraints that the financial mechanism exists to\nrelieve, consistent with paragraph 4 of Article 20 of the Convention.]\n10 Decision 16/4, annex.\n\n[11 Direct access for organizations of indigenous peoples and local communities include application of procedures for screening\nthe capacities, experience and performance of organizations in managing funds and implementing projects, according to established\nGlobal Environment Facility procedures and following approval by the operational focal points of the Global Environment Facility,\nwhich is granted in coordination with the national focal point for the Convention.]\n12 [Direct access for organizations of indigenous peoples and local communities include application of procedures for screening\n\nthe capacities, experience and performance of organizations in managing funds and implementing projects, according to\nestablished Global Environment Facility procedures and following approval by the operational focal points of the Global\nEnvironment Facility, which is granted in coordination with the national focal point for the Convention.]\n\n                                                                                                                            3/14","blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日</p>"},{"md":"私部門投資與金融流動，包括透過長期賦能政策框架、激勵措施、法規、混合型金融工具，以及開發具財務可行性且具備投資條件之生物多樣性金融計畫與案源；同時承認此類投資與公共財政具有互補性；\n(c) 在適當且符合國家情況下，促進全社會與全政府之方法，以強化國家層級之計畫與專案自主權，並使生物多樣性行動與國家所確定之優先事項、國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家發展優先事項及政策一致性相結合；\n(d) 持續改善其資源配置系統[9] [[，包括透過持續極大化全球環境效益之產生，並承認原住民族與地方社區在達成該等效益中所扮演的角色，以及改善其執行實體之配置績效] [藉由增進透明度、公平性、可預測性，並對開發中國家締約方（包括小島嶼開發中國家與低度開發國家）之[相關][特定]需求與優先事項之回應能力]];\n(e) 透過降低交易成本、簡化現有全球環境基金焦點領域與融資窗口之取得程序，[包括透過國家執行機構之直接取得模式，] 並改善財務支援之及時性與可預測性以撥付至受援國之首筆款項日期為衡量標準，藉此對所有符合資格之締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家[及環境最脆弱之國家]提供持續且強化之支援；\n(f) 深化對原住民族與地方社區之可取得性支援，以符合《公約》第八條第 (j) 款工作計畫之第八要素，以及《公約》其他與原住民族與地方社區相關之規定至 2030 年¹⁰（包括針對原住民族與地方社區用於生物多樣性保育、復育與永續利用之資金取得，包含直接取得），包括透過針對原住民族與地方社區 20% 全組合目標制定指南，其中包含[專屬][[直接]取得][11]模式；\n[(g) 根據相關締約方之國內立法，強化原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之全面、公平、包容、有效且具性別回應性之參與，[包括在決策過程中的參與];]\n(h) 持續促進由國家驅動之國家倡議，以及區域協調之區域與多國倡議[, 包括跨境倡議，並具備[公約國家焦點與相關國家主管機關]之有效參與 [與正式核准] [以及全球環境基金執行焦點之正式核准]];\n(i) 確保全球環境基金對執行《公約》之支援[, 包括[透過直接取得 [12] ]支援國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫之執行、監測、更新與審查，] 是由國家主導，並與[國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫以及]綱要之目標相一致；","html":"<p>私部門投資與金融流動，包括透過長期賦能政策框架、激勵措施、法規、混合型金融工具，以及開發具財務可行性且具備投資條件之生物多樣性金融計畫與案源；同時承認此類投資與公共財政具有互補性；<br />\n(c) 在適當且符合國家情況下，促進全社會與全政府之方法，以強化國家層級之計畫與專案自主權，並使生物多樣性行動與國家所確定之優先事項、國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家發展優先事項及政策一致性相結合；<br />\n(d) 持續改善其資源配置系統[9] [[，包括透過持續極大化全球環境效益之產生，並承認原住民族與地方社區在達成該等效益中所扮演的角色，以及改善其執行實體之配置績效] [藉由增進透明度、公平性、可預測性，並對開發中國家締約方（包括小島嶼開發中國家與低度開發國家）之[相關][特定]需求與優先事項之回應能力]];<br />\n(e) 透過降低交易成本、簡化現有全球環境基金焦點領域與融資窗口之取得程序，[包括透過國家執行機構之直接取得模式，] 並改善財務支援之及時性與可預測性以撥付至受援國之首筆款項日期為衡量標準，藉此對所有符合資格之締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家[及環境最脆弱之國家]提供持續且強化之支援；<br />\n(f) 深化對原住民族與地方社區之可取得性支援，以符合《公約》第八條第 (j) 款工作計畫之第八要素，以及《公約》其他與原住民族與地方社區相關之規定至 2030 年¹⁰（包括針對原住民族與地方社區用於生物多樣性保育、復育與永續利用之資金取得，包含直接取得），包括透過針對原住民族與地方社區 20% 全組合目標制定指南，其中包含[專屬][[直接]取得][11]模式；<br />\n[(g) 根據相關締約方之國內立法，強化原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之全面、公平、包容、有效且具性別回應性之參與，[包括在決策過程中的參與];]<br />\n(h) 持續促進由國家驅動之國家倡議，以及區域協調之區域與多國倡議[, 包括跨境倡議，並具備[公約國家焦點與相關國家主管機關]之有效參與 [與正式核准] [以及全球環境基金執行焦點之正式核准]];<br />\n(i) 確保全球環境基金對執行《公約》之支援[, 包括[透過直接取得 [12] ]支援國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫之執行、監測、更新與審查，] 是由國家主導，並與[國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫以及]綱要之目標相一致；</p>"},{"md":"[9 確保配置公式中任何以績效為基礎之要素（包括任何對過去撥款量之衡量），不會對其撥款率反映出財務機制旨在緩解之能力限制的締約方造成不利，此應與《公約》第二十條第四段保持一致。]\n10 決議 16/4，附件。\n[11 原住民族與地方社區組織之直接取得，包括根據既定之全球環境基金程序，申請對組織在管理資金與執行專案方面之能力、經驗與績效進行篩選，並在與公約國家焦點協調下，經全球環境基金執行焦點核准後進行。]\n12 [原住民族與地方社區組織之直接取得，包括根據既定之全球環境基金程序，申請對組織在管理資金與執行專案方面之能力、經驗與績效進行篩選，並在與公約國家焦點協調下，經全球環境基金執行焦點核准後進行。]","html":"<p>[9 確保配置公式中任何以績效為基礎之要素（包括任何對過去撥款量之衡量），不會對其撥款率反映出財務機制旨在緩解之能力限制的締約方造成不利，此應與《公約》第二十條第四段保持一致。]<br />\n10 決議 16/4，附件。<br />\n[11 原住民族與地方社區組織之直接取得，包括根據既定之全球環境基金程序，申請對組織在管理資金與執行專案方面之能力、經驗與績效進行篩選，並在與公約國家焦點協調下，經全球環境基金執行焦點核准後進行。]<br />\n12 [原住民族與地方社區組織之直接取得，包括根據既定之全球環境基金程序，申請對組織在管理資金與執行專案方面之能力、經驗與績效進行篩選，並在與公約國家焦點協調下，經全球環境基金執行焦點核准後進行。]</p>"}]},{"p":"p004","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae094e458b9a83bc4d4c2ff/p004.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 3 – 27 October 2026\n\n             (j)     Continuing to support the development and implementation of national biodiversity\n       finance plans or similar instruments and their integration, where applicable, into national policies\n       and priorities;\n             (k) Continuing to advance collaboration, coherence and complementarity across\n       multilateral climate funds and other sources of finance relevant to the implementation of the\n       Framework;\n            (l)    Strengthening national institutional and technical capacities for project preparation,\n       implementation, monitoring and reporting;\n              [(m) Simplifying project development guidance;]\n             (n) Reporting on the attainment of the targets mentioned in paragraph 9 above and on\n       disaggregated data on programming, approvals and disbursement by recipient country or region;\n             [(o) Improving the transparency and granularity of reporting on biodiversity-related finance,\n       including by distinguishing between financing for which biodiversity is a principal objective and\n       financing for which it is a significant objective under the Rio marker methodology, taking into\n       account the qualitative nature of the Rio markers and by clarifying the extent to which such financing\n       contribute to the implementation of the Framework;]\n               13. Also requests the Global Environment Facility to report to the Conference of the Parties\n       at its eighteenth meeting on the resources of the biodiversity focal area for the ninth replenishment\n       period of its Trust Fund expressed in United States dollars at the final replenishment level, together\n       with the corresponding figure for the eighth replenishment period, and on the share of resources\n       originally programmed and subsequently disbursed to small island developing States, presented\n       separately from least developed countries;\n             14. Recognizes the value of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund in complementing the\n       Global Environment Facility Trust Fund by providing financial support to eligible developing\n       country Parties for achieving the goals and targets of the Framework;\n             15. Welcomes the progress made by the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund with a one-step\n       approval process and the achievement to date of the three portfolio targets set forth in the Global\n       Biodiversity Framework Fund Programming Directions document13;\n             16. Takes note of the information on the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund contained in\n       the report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility for the seventeenth meeting of the\n       Conference of the Parties;\n             16bis. Recall paragraph 14 of decision 16/33, emphasizing the need to further scale up new\n       and additional resources from all sources to commensurate with the ambition of the Kunming-\n       Montreal Global Biodiversity Fund, in accordance with decision 15/15, paragraphs 19 and 20, while\n       recognizing that many eligible Parties have not yet received support from the Fund\n             17. Reiterates the call made by the council of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund at its\n       sixth meeting for new and additional contributions from all sources to support the continuous, rapid\n       and robust capitalization of the Fund, in line with Target 19 of the Kunming-Montreal Global\n       Biodiversity Framework, and without affecting existing obligations under article 20 of the\n       Convention;\n              18. Requests the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund to enhance efforts to mobilize\n       predictable, adequate and additional resources from all sources and report on the implementation of\n       its resource mobilization strategy for the period from July 2026 to June 2030, including through\n       disaggregated information on pledges and paid contributions by sources of finance;\n\n\n13 Programming Directions for the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund, GEF/C.64/06/Rev/01, 29 June 2023\n\n\n\n4/14","blocks":[{"md":"非正式文件，關於議程項目 8 (b) – 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日","html":"<p>非正式文件，關於議程項目 8 (b) – 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日</p>"},{"md":"(j)\n持續支持國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具的制定與實施，並在適用情況下將其納入國家政策與優先事項；\n(k) 持續促進多邊氣候基金與其他與實施綱要相關之財務來源之間的協作、一致性與互補性；\n(l) 加強國家在計畫準備、實施、監測與報告方面的制度與技術能力；\n[(m) 簡化計畫開發指南；]\n(n) 就上述第 9 段所述目標之達成情況，以及按受援國家或區域分類之規劃、核准與撥款的細分資料進行報告；\n[(o) 提高生物多樣性相關財務報告的透明度與細粒度，包括根據里約標記（Rio marker）方法論，區分以生物多樣性為主要目標的融資與以生物多樣性為重要目標的融資，並考量里約標記的性質，且澄清此類融資對實施綱要的貢獻程度；]","html":"<p>(j)<br />\n持續支持國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具的制定與實施，並在適用情況下將其納入國家政策與優先事項；<br />\n(k) 持續促進多邊氣候基金與其他與實施綱要相關之財務來源之間的協作、一致性與互補性；<br />\n(l) 加強國家在計畫準備、實施、監測與報告方面的制度與技術能力；<br />\n[(m) 簡化計畫開發指南；]<br />\n(n) 就上述第 9 段所述目標之達成情況，以及按受援國家或區域分類之規劃、核准與撥款的細分資料進行報告；<br />\n[(o) 提高生物多樣性相關財務報告的透明度與細粒度，包括根據里約標記（Rio marker）方法論，區分以生物多樣性為主要目標的融資與以生物多樣性為重要目標的融資，並考量里約標記的性質，且澄清此類融資對實施綱要的貢獻程度；]</p>"},{"md":"13. 亦**請求**全球環境基金在第十八次締約方大會上，就其信託基金第九期增資期間，以最終增補水平表示之美元計價的生物多樣性重點領域資源，連同第八期增資期間的相應數字，以及原先規劃並隨後撥付給小島嶼開發中國家的資源比例進行報告，且此項報告應與低度開發國家的報告分開呈現；","html":"<p>13. 亦<strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金在第十八次締約方大會上，就其信託基金第九期增資期間，以最終增補水平表示之美元計價的生物多樣性重點領域資源，連同第八期增資期間的相應數字，以及原先規劃並隨後撥付給小島嶼開發中國家的資源比例進行報告，且此項報告應與低度開發國家的報告分開呈現；</p>"},{"md":"14. **認可**全球生物多樣性綱要基金在補充全球環境基金信託基金方面的價值，透過為符合條件的開發中國家締約方提供財務支持，以實現綱要的目標與指標；","html":"<p>14. <strong>認可</strong>全球生物多樣性綱要基金在補充全球環境基金信託基金方面的價值，透過為符合條件的開發中國家締約方提供財務支持，以實現綱要的目標與指標；</p>"},{"md":"15. **歡迎**全球生物多樣性綱要基金透過單一步驟核准程序所取得的進展，以及迄今為止在「全球生物多樣性綱要基金規劃指南」¹³中所設定的三項投資組合目標之達成情況；","html":"<p>15. <strong>歡迎</strong>全球生物多樣性綱要基金透過單一步驟核准程序所取得的進展，以及迄今為止在「全球生物多樣性綱要基金規劃指南」¹³中所設定的三項投資組合目標之達成情況；</p>"},{"md":"16. **注意到**全球環境基金理事會報告中關於全球生物多樣性綱要基金的資訊，該報告係針對第十七次締約方大會；","html":"<p>16. <strong>注意到</strong>全球環境基金理事會報告中關於全球生物多樣性綱要基金的資訊，該報告係針對第十七次締約方大會；</p>"},{"md":"16bis. **回顧**決議 16/33 第 14 段，強調根據決議 15/15 第 19 及 20 段，有必要進一步擴大來自所有來源的新增與額外資源，以與昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要的雄心相稱，同時認可許多符合條件的締約方尚未獲得該基金的支持；","html":"<p>16bis. <strong>回顧</strong>決議 16/33 第 14 段，強調根據決議 15/15 第 19 及 20 段，有必要進一步擴大來自所有來源的新增與額外資源，以與昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要的雄心相稱，同時認可許多符合條件的締約方尚未獲得該基金的支持；</p>"},{"md":"17. **重申**全球生物多樣性綱要基金理事會在第六次會議上所提出的呼籲，即要求來自所有來源的新增與額外捐助，以支持該基金持續、快速且穩健的資本化，此舉應符合昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要的目標 19，且不影響《公約》第二十條下的現有義務；","html":"<p>17. <strong>重申</strong>全球生物多樣性綱要基金理事會在第六次會議上所提出的呼籲，即要求來自所有來源的新增與額外捐助，以支持該基金持續、快速且穩健的資本化，此舉應符合昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要的目標 19，且不影響《公約》第二十條下的現有義務；</p>"},{"md":"18. **請求**全球生物多樣性綱要基金加強努力，從所有來源動員可預測、充足且額外的資源，並報告其 2026 年 7 月至 2030 年 6 月期間資源動員策略的實施情況，包括透過按財務來源分類的承諾與已付捐助之細分資訊；","html":"<p>18. <strong>請求</strong>全球生物多樣性綱要基金加強努力，從所有來源動員可預測、充足且額外的資源，並報告其 2026 年 7 月至 2030 年 6 月期間資源動員策略的實施情況，包括透過按財務來源分類的承諾與已付捐助之細分資訊；</p>"},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />"},{"md":"¹³ 全球生物多樣性綱要基金規劃指南，GEF/C.64/06/Rev/01，2023 年 6 月 29 日","html":"<p>¹³ 全球生物多樣性綱要基金規劃指南，GEF/C.64/06/Rev/01，2023 年 6 月 29 日</p>"}]},{"p":"p005","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae094e458b9a83bc4d4c2ff/p005.md","en":"                                                            Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 3 – 27 October 2026\n\n              19. Invites developed country Parties and Parties that voluntarily assume the obligations of\n        developed country Parties, other governments at all levels, the private sector and philanthropic\n        organizations to make or increase their contributions to the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund;\n              20. Requests the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund and its implementing agencies to\n        continue to enhance its efforts to:\n              (a) Facilitate, as appropriate, the mobilization of financial resources from all sources,\n        recognizing the need for further capitalization;\n                (b) Improve co-financing arrangements as appropriate, whilst recognizing that co-financing is\n        not a requirement, and without creating additional barriers to access or shifting the financial burden\n        to all eligible countries, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States,\n        also taking into consideration the specific needs of vulnerable countries, in the context of paragraph\n        6 and 7 of article 20;\n              (c) Reduce, where appropriate and taking into account country ownership, project cylcle\n        processing times, including for the disbursement and endorsement processes of approved projects\n        though transparent, predictable and timebound procedures, and streamline implementation;\n              (f)    Report on average processing and disbursement times disaggregated for least developed\n        countries and small island developing States, and other eligible Parties by region;\n               [(h) Enhance equitable access, including by considering measures to facilitate access for\n        eligible country Parties that have not yet received support from the Global Biodiversity Framework\n        Fund;]]\n               21. Requests the Global Environment Facility, in collaboration with the Executive Secretary\n        of the Convention [as appropriate] [, to consider supporting,][to provide support to] [all] eligible\n        Parties in line with its mandate, for:\n              [21 Alt1.     Requests the Global Environment Facility, in collaboration with the Executive\n        Secretary of the Convention, [as appropriate[,] [and]] within their respective mandates [as\n        appropriate], to provide support[, as appropriate,] to [all] eligible Parties for:]\n              [21 Alt2.    Requests the Global Environment Facility, in collaboration with the Executive\n        Secretary of the Convention, within their respective mandates, to provide support to eligible Parties\n        for:]\n               (a) Project preparation and tracking ongoing biodiversity funding needs, gaps and priorities,\n        as necessary, including where applicable through national coordination mechanisms such as country\n        platforms or national steering committees;\n               [(b) Capacity-building and readiness support for national implementing agencies, including\n        for accreditation;]\n             (c) The preparation and submission of national reports on the implementation of the\n        Convention, the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety14 and the Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic\n        Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their Utilization, taking into\n        account national circumstances;15\n              (d) Capacity-building for leveraging private sector financing, including from capital\n        markets, through, inter alia, innovative mechanisms and blended finance, and for developing\n        financially viable projects, with robust safeguards[ to avoid increasing debt vulnerabilities];\n              22. Requests the Executive Secretary to undertake preparatory work for the stocktake\n        review of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund referred to in paragraph 29 of decision 15/15,[\n        in accordance with annex III to the present decision], in conjunction with its seventh quadrennial\n14 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619.\n15 Ibid., vol. 3008, No. 30619.\n\n\n\n                                                                                                             5/14","blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日</p>"},{"md":"19. **邀請**已開發國家締約方、自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之締約方、各級其他政府、私部門及慈善組織，對全球生物多樣性綱要基金進行或增加其貢獻；","html":"<p>19. <strong>邀請</strong>已開發國家締約方、自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之締約方、各級其他政府、私部門及慈善組織，對全球生物多樣性綱要基金進行或增加其貢獻；</p>"},{"md":"20. **請求**全球生物多樣性綱要基金及其執行機構繼續加強其努力以：\n    (a) 在適當情況下，促進來自所有來源之財務資源動員，並承認進一步增資之必要性；\n    (b) 在適當情況下，改善共同融資安排，同時承認共同融資並非必要條件，且不應造成額外的取得障礙，或將財務負擔轉嫁至所有符合資格之國家，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，並在第 20 條第 6 段及第 7 段之脈絡下，亦考慮脆弱國家之特定需求；\n    (c) 在適當情況下且考量國家自主權的前提下，透過透明、可預測且有時限之程序，縮短專案週期之處理時間，包括核准專案之撥款與認可程序，並簡化執行流程；\n    (f) 針對低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及其他符合資格之締約方，按區域分別報告平均處理與撥款時間；\n    [(h) 加強公平取得，包括考慮採取措施，以促進尚未獲得全球生物多樣性綱要基金支持之符合資格締約方之取得；]]","html":"<p>20. <strong>請求</strong>全球生物多樣性綱要基金及其執行機構繼續加強其努力以：<br />\n    (a) 在適當情況下，促進來自所有來源之財務資源動員，並承認進一步增資之必要性；<br />\n    (b) 在適當情況下，改善共同融資安排，同時承認共同融資並非必要條件，且不應造成額外的取得障礙，或將財務負擔轉嫁至所有符合資格之國家，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，並在第 20 條第 6 段及第 7 段之脈絡下，亦考慮脆弱國家之特定需求；<br />\n    (c) 在適當情況下且考量國家自主權的前提下，透過透明、可預測且有時限之程序，縮短專案週期之處理時間，包括核准專案之撥款與認可程序，並簡化執行流程；<br />\n    (f) 針對低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及其他符合資格之締約方，按區域分別報告平均處理與撥款時間；<br />\n    [(h) 加強公平取得，包括考慮採取措施，以促進尚未獲得全球生物多樣性綱要基金支持之符合資格締約方之取得；]]</p>"},{"md":"21. **請求**全球環境基金與《公約》執行秘書[於適當情況下]合作[，考慮提供支持，][以向][所有]符合資格之締約方，依其職權，提供以下方面之支持：\n    [21 Alt1.\n    **請求**全球環境基金與《公約》執行秘書合作，[於適當情況下[，][且]]在其各自職權範圍內[於適當情況下]，向[所有]符合資格之締約方提供[適當之]支持，以用於：]\n    [21 Alt2.\n    **請求**全球環境基金與《公約》執行秘書合作，在其各自職權範圍內，向符合資格之締約方提供支持，以用於：]\n    (a) 專案準備，以及視必要情況追蹤持續進行中之生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項，包括在適用時透過國家協調機制（如國家平台或國家指導委員會）進行；\n    [(b) 為國家執行機構提供能力建構與準備支持，包括認證支持；]\n    (c) 考量國家情況，編製並提交關於執行《公約》、卡塔赫納生物安全議定書$^{14}$以及《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其後所產生利益之名古屋議定書》之國家報告$^{15}$；\n    (d) 透過（除其他外）創新機制與混合金融，為槓桿化私部門融資（包括來自資本市場之資金）提供能力建構，以及開發具財務可行性且具備穩健保障措施[以避免增加債務脆弱性]之專案；","html":"<p>21. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金與《公約》執行秘書[於適當情況下]合作[，考慮提供支持，][以向][所有]符合資格之締約方，依其職權，提供以下方面之支持：<br />\n    [21 Alt1.<br />\n<strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金與《公約》執行秘書合作，[於適當情況下[，][且]]在其各自職權範圍內[於適當情況下]，向[所有]符合資格之締約方提供[適當之]支持，以用於：]<br />\n    [21 Alt2.<br />\n<strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金與《公約》執行秘書合作，在其各自職權範圍內，向符合資格之締約方提供支持，以用於：]<br />\n    (a) 專案準備，以及視必要情況追蹤持續進行中之生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項，包括在適用時透過國家協調機制（如國家平台或國家指導委員會）進行；<br />\n    [(b) 為國家執行機構提供能力建構與準備支持，包括認證支持；]<br />\n    (c) 考量國家情況，編製並提交關於執行《公約》、卡塔赫納生物安全議定書<sup>14</sup>以及《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其後所產生利益之名古屋議定書》之國家報告<sup>15</sup>；<br />\n    (d) 透過（除其他外）創新機制與混合金融，為槓桿化私部門融資（包括來自資本市場之資金）提供能力建構，以及開發具財務可行性且具備穩健保障措施[以避免增加債務脆弱性]之專案；</p>"},{"md":"22. **請求**執行秘書配合決議 15/15 第 29 段所指稱之全球生物多樣性綱要基金盤點審查，[依據本決議附件 III]，與其第七次四年一度之","html":"<p>22. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書配合決議 15/15 第 29 段所指稱之全球生物多樣性綱要基金盤點審查，[依據本決議附件 III]，與其第七次四年一度之</p>"},{"md":"---\n$^{14}$ 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。\n$^{15}$ 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>14</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n<sup>15</sup> 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。</p>"}]},{"p":"p006","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae094e458b9a83bc4d4c2ff/p006.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 3 – 27 October 2026\n\n       review of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism, [recognizing that the stocktake shall inform,\n       but not prejudge, consideration by the Conference of the Parties of the future institutional structure\n       of the financial mechanism provided under Article 21 of the Convention];\n              [23. Invites the Global Environment Facility to facilitate financial support for eligible Parties\n       that have not yet received support for the development of the national biodiversity strategies and\n       action plans and national targets or the preparation of national reports;]\n              [(g) Provide necessary resources, fully disbursed allocated funds to [recipient countries]\n       [beneficiaries] [well] before [reporting deadline] [reporting period], and complete organizational\n       work, [including at the national level], in support of the preparation of the eighth national reports by\n       the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;]\n              [24. Requests the Global Environment Facility, in consultation with recipient countries and\n       the Executive Secretary, to review the effectiveness of projects funded during its seventh and eighth\n       cycles for the development of national biodiversity strategies and actions plans and national reports\n       [under the Convention and its Protocols] and to report on the measures that it has taken to address\n       identified challenges [for][to adjust accordingly] the preparation of the eight national report [to the\n       Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before][at] the eighteenth meeting of the\n       Conference of the Parties;]\n              25. [Requests that specific resources be reserved for][Encourages developing country\n       Parties to the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety to submit to the Global Environment Facility]\n       biosafety projects under the Protocol, given the small number of such projects funded in previous\n       rounds;\n              26. Requests the Executive Secretary, in consultation with the Secretariat of the Global\n       Environment Facility, to prepare a draft four-year outcome-oriented framework of biodiversity\n       programme priorities of the Convention and its Protocols related to the use of Facility resources for\n       biodiversity for the period from July 2030 to June 2034, taking into consideration the global review\n       of collective progress in the implementation of the Framework, [and addressing expressly the access\n       modalities and capacity constraints of developing countries Parties, in particular least developed\n       countries and small island developing States, consistent with paragraphs 5 and 6 of Article 20 of the\n       Convention,] for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before\n       the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties and subsequent adoption by the Conference\n       of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting;\n              [27. Emphasizes that the preparation of the four-year outcome-oriented framework of\n       biodiversity programme priorities of the Convention and its Protocols for the tenth replenishment\n       period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund is without prejudice to the process established\n       in decision 16/34 regarding the institutional structure for the financial mechanism provided under\n       Article 21 of the Convention.]\n              28. Adopts the additional guidance to the Global Environment Facility contained in annex I\n       to the present decision, and requests the Council of the Global Environment Facility to include\n       information regarding the implementation of the additional guidance in its reports to the Conference\n       of the Parties;\n             29. Notes the information on funding needs received from 45 eligible Parties and the\n       compilation and analysis of that information transmitted by the Secretariat of the Convention on\n       Biological Diversity to the Global Environment Facility to help with the negotiations for the ninth\n       replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund;\n\n\n\n\n6/14","blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日</p>"},{"md":"財務機制有效性之審查，[認可該盤點應為締約方大會考量《公約》第 21 條規定之財務機制未來制度結構提供資訊，但不應預設其結果]；","html":"<p>財務機制有效性之審查，[認可該盤點應為締約方大會考量《公約》第 21 條規定之財務機制未來制度結構提供資訊，但不應預設其結果]；</p>"},{"md":"[23. 邀請全球環境基金促進對符合條件之締約方之財務支持，該等締約方尚未獲得用於制定國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家目標，或編製國家報告之支持；]","html":"<p>[23. 邀請全球環境基金促進對符合條件之締約方之財務支持，該等締約方尚未獲得用於制定國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家目標，或編製國家報告之支持；]</p>"},{"md":"[(g) 提供必要資源，將已分配之資金全額撥付予 [受援國] [受益方] [於] [報告截止日期] [報告期間] 之前，並完成 [包括在國家層級] 之組織工作，以支持在第十八次締約方大會召開前完成第八次國家報告之工作；]","html":"<p>[(g) 提供必要資源，將已分配之資金全額撥付予 [受援國] [受益方] [於] [報告截止日期] [報告期間] 之前，並完成 [包括在國家層級] 之組織工作，以支持在第十八次締約方大會召開前完成第八次國家報告之工作；]</p>"},{"md":"[24. 請求全球環境基金在諮詢受援國與執行秘書後，審查其第七與第八週期期間，為制定國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家報告 [於《公約》及其議定書下] 所資助之專案有效性，並報告其為應對已識別之挑戰 [為][以進行相應調整] 而採取之措施，[於第十八次締約方大會召開前召開之執行附屬機構會議][於] 第十八次締約方大會，提交第八次國家報告之編製；]","html":"<p>[24. 請求全球環境基金在諮詢受援國與執行秘書後，審查其第七與第八週期期間，為制定國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家報告 [於《公約》及其議定書下] 所資助之專案有效性，並報告其為應對已識別之挑戰 [為][以進行相應調整] 而採取之措施，[於第十八次締約方大會召開前召開之執行附屬機構會議][於] 第十八次締約方大會，提交第八次國家報告之編製；]</p>"},{"md":"25. [請求為議定書下之生物安全專案保留特定資源][鼓勵卡塔赫納生物安全議定書之開發中國家締約方向全球環境基金提交] 議定書下之生物安全專案，鑑於先前輪次資助此類專案之數量較少；","html":"<p>25. [請求為議定書下之生物安全專案保留特定資源][鼓勵卡塔赫納生物安全議定書之開發中國家締約方向全球環境基金提交] 議定書下之生物安全專案，鑑於先前輪次資助此類專案之數量較少；</p>"},{"md":"26. 請求執行秘書在諮詢全球環境基金秘書處後，準備一份關於《公約》及其議定書生物多樣性計畫優先事項之四年期成果導向架構草案，該架構與 2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月期間利用基金資源用於生物多樣性之事項相關，並應考量對《綱要》實施集體進展之全球審查，[並明確應對開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家的取得模式與能力限制，且須符合《公約》第 20 條第 5 及第 6 段]，以供執行附屬機構在第十八次締約方大會召開前召開之會議審議，並由締約方大會於其第十八次會議隨後採納；","html":"<p>26. 請求執行秘書在諮詢全球環境基金秘書處後，準備一份關於《公約》及其議定書生物多樣性計畫優先事項之四年期成果導向架構草案，該架構與 2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月期間利用基金資源用於生物多樣性之事項相關，並應考量對《綱要》實施集體進展之全球審查，[並明確應對開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家的取得模式與能力限制，且須符合《公約》第 20 條第 5 及第 6 段]，以供執行附屬機構在第十八次締約方大會召開前召開之會議審議，並由締約方大會於其第十八次會議隨後採納；</p>"},{"md":"[27. 強調為全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期準備《公約》及其議定書生物多樣性計畫優先事項之四年期成果導向架構，不影響決議 16/34 中關於《公約》第 21 條規定之財務機制制度結構所建立之程序。]","html":"<p>[27. 強調為全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期準備《公約》及其議定書生物多樣性計畫優先事項之四年期成果導向架構，不影響決議 16/34 中關於《公約》第 21 條規定之財務機制制度結構所建立之程序。]</p>"},{"md":"28. 採納本決議附件一所載之給予全球環境基金之附加指南，並請求全球環境基金理事會在向締約方大會提交之報告中，納入有關實施該附加指南之資訊；","html":"<p>28. 採納本決議附件一所載之給予全球環境基金之附加指南，並請求全球環境基金理事會在向締約方大會提交之報告中，納入有關實施該附加指南之資訊；</p>"},{"md":"29. 注意到從 45 個符合條件之締約方收到之關於資金需求之資訊，以及由生物多樣性公約秘書處傳送予全球環境基金之該等資訊之彙編與分析，以協助全球環境基金信託基金第九次增補之談判；","html":"<p>29. 注意到從 45 個符合條件之締約方收到之關於資金需求之資訊，以及由生物多樣性公約秘書處傳送予全球環境基金之該等資訊之彙編與分析，以協助全球環境基金信託基金第九次增補之談判；</p>"}]},{"p":"p007","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae094e458b9a83bc4d4c2ff/p007.md","en":"                                                            Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 3 – 27 October 2026\n\n            30. Takes note of the report on the assessment of the amount of funds needed for the\n      implementation of the Convention and its Protocols for the ninth replenishment period of the Global\n      Environment Facility Trust Fund;16\n             31. Notes the limited number of submissions from eligible Parties and therefore limited\n      information available for assessing the amount of funds needed for the implementation of the\n      Convention and its Protocols and the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework for the\n      ninth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund;\n            [32. Also notes the importance of a realistic assessment of funding necessary and available\n      for the implementation of the Convention and its Protocols and the Framework for the ninth\n      replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility;]\n             [33. Emphasizes the need to strengthen technical and institutional support for eligible Parties,\n      so that their needs are fully reflected in future assessments;]\n             [34. Adopts the terms of reference for a full assessment of the amount of funds that are\n      necessary to assist developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small\n      island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in accordance with the guidance\n      provided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling their commitments under the Convention for\n      the tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (July 2030–June\n      2034), as contained in annex II to the present decision, noting that the assessment should be\n      conducted in a manner that avoids disproportionate administrative burdens and provides for financial\n      and technical support for data collection in developing country Parties;]\n            [35. Encourages Parties to establish national platforms for planning and monitoring\n      biodiversity projects that and are accessible to stakeholders and regularly updated;]\n             [36. Adopts the terms of reference for the seventh quadrennial review of the effectiveness of\n      the financial mechanism, as contained in annex III to the present decision;]\n             37. Invites Parties, other Governments and relevant organizations, as well as indigenous\n      peoples and local communities, women and youth, to contribute to and participate in the seventh\n      quadrennial review of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism, as outlined in the terms of\n      reference;\n             38. Emphasizes the importance of integrating [in the quadrennial review] specific indicators\n      for eligible Parties, in particular on the number of projects funded, disbursement times and impact\n      on local communities;\n             39.       Requests the Executive Secretary[, subject to availability of resources]:\n              [(a) To commission and make available a report on the seventh quadrennial review of the\n      effectiveness of the financial mechanism in time for consideration by the Conference of the Parties\n      at its eighteenth meeting;]\n             (b) To prepare a report on the full assessment of the amount of funds that are necessary to\n      assist developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island\n      developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in accordance with the guidance\n      provided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling their commitments under the Convention for\n      the tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund, for consideration by\n      the Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the\n      Conference of the Parties and by the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting;\n            [(c) To further strengthen collaboration and engagement with financial institutions and\n      stakeholders, especially those recognized by the Global Environment Facility, the Green Climate\n      Fund and the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development, in order to accelerate the\n\n16 CBD/SBI/6/INF/13.\n\n\n\n                                                                                                            7/14","blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2","html":"<p>關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2</p>"},{"md":"30. **注意到**關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間，為執行《公約》及其議定書所需資金金額評估之報告；16\n31. **注意到**符合資格之締約方提交之報告數量有限，因此對於評估全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間，為執行《公約》及其議定書與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》所需之資金金額，可用資訊有限；\n[32. **亦注意到**針對全球環境基金第九期增資期間，對執行《公約》及其議定書與《綱要》所需且可用之資金進行務實評估的重要性；]\n[33. **強調**有必要加強對符合資格締約方的技術與制度支持，以使其需求能充分反映在未來的評估中；]\n[34. **採納**本決議附件 II 所載之職權範圍，針對全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月），依據締約方所提供之指引，就為協助開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）以及轉型經濟體締約方履行其在《公約》下之承諾所需之資金金額進行全面評估之職權範圍；並注意到該評估應以避免不成比例之行政負擔之方式進行，並為開發中國家締約方之資料收集提供財務與技術支持；]\n[35. **鼓勵**締約方建立生物多樣性計畫之國家平台，且該平台應為利害關係人所能使用並定期更新；]\n[36. **採納**本決議附件 III 所載之財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之職權範圍；]\n37. **邀請**締約方、其他政府與相關組織，以及原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，依據職權範圍所述，為財務機制有效性之第七次四年一度審查做出貢獻並參與其中；\n38. **強調**在 [四年一度審查中] 納入符合資格締約方之特定指標的重要性，特別是關於資助計畫數量、撥款時間以及對地方社區之影響；\n39. **請求**執行秘書[在資源可用之情況下]：","html":"<p>30. <strong>注意到</strong>關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間，為執行《公約》及其議定書所需資金金額評估之報告；16<br />\n31. <strong>注意到</strong>符合資格之締約方提交之報告數量有限，因此對於評估全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間，為執行《公約》及其議定書與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》所需之資金金額，可用資訊有限；<br />\n[32. <strong>亦注意到</strong>針對全球環境基金第九期增資期間，對執行《公約》及其議定書與《綱要》所需且可用之資金進行務實評估的重要性；]<br />\n[33. <strong>強調</strong>有必要加強對符合資格締約方的技術與制度支持，以使其需求能充分反映在未來的評估中；]<br />\n[34. <strong>採納</strong>本決議附件 II 所載之職權範圍，針對全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月），依據締約方所提供之指引，就為協助開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）以及轉型經濟體締約方履行其在《公約》下之承諾所需之資金金額進行全面評估之職權範圍；並注意到該評估應以避免不成比例之行政負擔之方式進行，並為開發中國家締約方之資料收集提供財務與技術支持；]<br />\n[35. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方建立生物多樣性計畫之國家平台，且該平台應為利害關係人所能使用並定期更新；]<br />\n[36. <strong>採納</strong>本決議附件 III 所載之財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之職權範圍；]<br />\n37. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府與相關組織，以及原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，依據職權範圍所述，為財務機制有效性之第七次四年一度審查做出貢獻並參與其中；<br />\n38. <strong>強調</strong>在 [四年一度審查中] 納入符合資格締約方之特定指標的重要性，特別是關於資助計畫數量、撥款時間以及對地方社區之影響；<br />\n39. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書[在資源可用之情況下]：</p>"},{"md":"[(a) 委託並及時提供一份關於財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之報告，以供締約方大會第十八次會議審議；]\n(b) 準備一份關於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間，依據締約方所提供之指引，就為協助開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）以及轉型經濟體締約方履行其在《公約》下之承諾所需之資金金額之全面評估報告，以供執行附屬機構在締約方大會第十八次會議召開前之會議審議，並供締約方大會第十八次會議審議；\n[(c) 進一步加強與金融機構及利害關係人之合作與參與，特別是那些獲得全球環境基金、綠色氣候基金及經濟合作暨發展組織認可之機構，以加速","html":"<p>[(a) 委託並及時提供一份關於財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之報告，以供締約方大會第十八次會議審議；]<br />\n(b) 準備一份關於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間，依據締約方所提供之指引，就為協助開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）以及轉型經濟體締約方履行其在《公約》下之承諾所需之資金金額之全面評估報告，以供執行附屬機構在締約方大會第十八次會議召開前之會議審議，並供締約方大會第十八次會議審議；<br />\n[(c) 進一步加強與金融機構及利害關係人之合作與參與，特別是那些獲得全球環境基金、綠色氣候基金及經濟合作暨發展組織認可之機構，以加速</p>"},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />"},{"md":"16 CBD/SBI/6/INF/13.","html":"<p>16 CBD/SBI/6/INF/13.</p>"}]},{"p":"p008","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae094e458b9a83bc4d4c2ff/p008.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 3 – 27 October 2026\n\n       implementation of the Framework, with an emphasis on improving access modalities[, including\n       direct access and [simplified][simplifying] procedures for developing country Parties], while\n       ensuring transparency, accountability, gender equality and the respect for human rights;]\n             [(d) To report on the results of the collaboration and engagement mentioned in the\n       subparagraph above, and include options for such engagements, to the Subsidiary Body on\n       Implementation at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;]\n             [(e) To facilitate the effective participation of indigenous peoples and local communities,\n       women and youth in the implementation of the activities referred to in subparagraphs (a) to (d)\n       above.]\n       Annex I\n       Additional guidance to the Global Environment Facility\n                       [Placeholder for elements of guidance]\n       Annex II\n       Terms of reference for a full assessment of the amount of funds that are necessary to\n       assist developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and\n       small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in\n       accordance with the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling\n       their commitments under the Convention for the tenth replenishment period of the\n       Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (July 2030–June 2034)\n       A.      Objective and scope\n       1.    The objective of the work to be carried out under the present terms of reference is to enable\n       the Conference of the Parties to the Convention on Biological Diversity17 to make an assessment of\n       the amount of funds that are necessary to assist developing country Parties, in particular the least\n       developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in\n       accordance with the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling their\n       commitments under the Convention and its Protocols, in particular the commitment to implementing\n       any successor to the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework 18 over the tenth\n       replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (July 2030–June 2034), and\n       determine the amount of resources needed, in accordance with paragraph 1 of Article 21 of the\n       Convention and decision III/8 of 15 November 1996 of the Conference of the Parties.\n       B.      Methodology\n       2.      The funding needs assessment should be conducted taking into account:\n               (a)     Article 20 and paragraph 1 of Article 21 of the Convention, as well as the Framework;\n            (b) Guidance provided to the financial mechanism by the Conference of the Parties, which\n       may call for future financial resources, and in the resource mobilization decision, in which the\n       Conference of the Parties calls for a broadening of the contributor base;\n             (c) All obligations under the Convention and its Protocols and relevant decisions adopted\n       by the Conference of the Parties, in particular the Framework;\n            (d) National strategies, plans or programmes developed in accordance with Article 6 of the\n       Convention and national biodiversity finance plans or similar instruments, where available;\n\n\n\n\n17 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.\n18 Decision 15/4, annex.\n\n\n\n8/14","blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日</p>"},{"md":"綱要之執行，重點在於改善取得模式[，包括針對開發中國家締約方之直接取得與[簡化][簡化]程序]，同時確保透明度、問責制、性別平等及對人權的尊重；]\n[(d) 向執行附屬機構報告上述次段落所述之合作與參與結果，並向其提供此類參與之選項，該報告應於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議提出；]\n[(e) 促進原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年有效參與上述 (a) 至 (d) 項所述活動之執行。]","html":"<p>綱要之執行，重點在於改善取得模式[，包括針對開發中國家締約方之直接取得與[簡化][簡化]程序]，同時確保透明度、問責制、性別平等及對人權的尊重；]<br />\n[(d) 向執行附屬機構報告上述次段落所述之合作與參與結果，並向其提供此類參與之選項，該報告應於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議提出；]<br />\n[(e) 促進原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年有效參與上述 (a) 至 (d) 項所述活動之執行。]</p>"},{"md":"附件 I\n給全球環境基金之額外指引\n[指引要素之預留位置]","html":"<p>附件 I<br />\n給全球環境基金之額外指引<br />\n[指引要素之預留位置]</p>"},{"md":"附件 II\n根據締約方大會所提供之指引，針對為協助開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及經濟轉型中締約方，於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）履行其在公約下之承諾，所需資金金額進行全面評估之任務說明書","html":"<p>附件 II<br />\n根據締約方大會所提供之指引，針對為協助開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及經濟轉型中締約方，於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）履行其在公約下之承諾，所需資金金額進行全面評估之任務說明書</p>"},{"md":"A.\n目標與範圍","html":"<p>A.<br />\n目標與範圍</p>"},{"md":"1.\n根據本任務說明書所進行之工作，其目標在於使生物多樣性公約<sup>17</sup>締約方大會能夠，根據締約方大會所提供之指引，針對為協助開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及經濟轉型中締約方，於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）履行其在公約及其議定書下之承諾，特別是履行任何昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要<sup>18</sup>繼任者之承諾，進行所需資金金額之評估，並根據公約第 21 條第 1 段及 1996 年 11 月 15 日締約方大會決議 III/8，確定所需資源之金額。","html":"<p>1.<br />\n根據本任務說明書所進行之工作，其目標在於使生物多樣性公約<sup>17</sup>締約方大會能夠，根據締約方大會所提供之指引，針對為協助開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及經濟轉型中締約方，於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）履行其在公約及其議定書下之承諾，特別是履行任何昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要<sup>18</sup>繼任者之承諾，進行所需資金金額之評估，並根據公約第 21 條第 1 段及 1996 年 11 月 15 日締約方大會決議 III/8，確定所需資源之金額。</p>"},{"md":"B.\n方法論","html":"<p>B.<br />\n方法論</p>"},{"md":"2.\n資金需求評估應考量：\n(a) 公約第 20 條及第 21 條第 1 段，以及綱要；","html":"<p>2.<br />\n資金需求評估應考量：<br />\n(a) 公約第 20 條及第 21 條第 1 段，以及綱要；</p>"},{"md":"(b) 締約方大會提供予財務機制之指引（該指引可能要求未來之財務資源），以及在要求擴大捐助者基礎之資源動員決議中之指引；\n(c) 公約及其議定書下之所有義務，以及締約方大會所通過之相關決議，特別是綱要；\n(d) 根據公約第 6 條所制定之國家策略、計畫或方案，以及國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具（若有）；","html":"<p>(b) 締約方大會提供予財務機制之指引（該指引可能要求未來之財務資源），以及在要求擴大捐助者基礎之資源動員決議中之指引；<br />\n(c) 公約及其議定書下之所有義務，以及締約方大會所通過之相關決議，特別是綱要；<br />\n(d) 根據公約第 6 條所制定之國家策略、計畫或方案，以及國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具（若有）；</p>"},{"md":"---\n<sup>17</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。\n<sup>18</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>17</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n<sup>18</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。</p>"}]},{"p":"p009","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae094e458b9a83bc4d4c2ff/p009.md","en":"                                                           Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 3 – 27 October 2026\n\n               (e) Information communicated to the Conference of the Parties in national reports and by\n        the Parties through the financial reporting framework and other submission responses to surveys and\n        interviews;\n              (f)   Policies and guidelines agreed by the Council of the Global Environment Facility for\n        determining eligibility for funding of projects;\n              (g) Synergies with other biodiversity-related conventions and other multilateral\n        environmental agreements funded by the Global Environment Facility, including those with respect\n        to operations and impacts;\n               (h) Additional private capital mobilized through blended finance, including through the use\n        of non-grant instruments, while recognizing the challenges that may be experienced by some Parties,\n        in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, in mobilizing private\n        capital in this regard;\n                (i)     Policy coherence;\n              (j)   Other relevant estimations, including the costs of implementing the Gender Plan of\n        Action (2023–2030);19\n              (k) Exchange rates, inflation and the incremental costs of the implementation of the\n        provisions of the Convention in developing countries.\n        3.    In the context of the assessment, interviews, surveys, quantitative and qualitative analyses, and\n        consultations should be undertaken, as needed for the preparation of the report, including:\n               (a) A compilation and analysis of the needs identified in national biodiversity strategies and\n        action plans and national biodiversity finance plans, including country-specific resource mobilization\n        strategies, prepared by Global Environment Facility-eligible and other relevant Parties pursuant to\n        Article 6 of the Convention, taking into account incremental cost funding as the fundamental\n        operational principle of the Global Environment Facility;\n               (b) A review of reports submitted by Parties pursuant to Articles 6 and 26 of the Convention,\n        as well as Article 33 of the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety20 and Article 29 of the Nagoya Protocol\n        on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their\n        Utilization, 21 to identify funding needs related to the fulfilment of their obligations under the\n        Convention and its Protocols;\n              (c) The estimated financial implications of guidance provided to the financial mechanism\n        by the Conference of the Parties;\n              (d) A compilation and analysis of any supplementary information provided by Global\n        Environment Facility-eligible Parties on their funding needs for the implementation of their\n        obligations under the Convention and its Protocols.\n        C.      Implementation\n        4.    The national focal points of the Convention and the focal points of the financial mechanism\n        should, as appropriate, bear joint responsibility for coordinating national-level incremental funding\n        needs assessments, in collaboration with relevant stakeholders and other focal points under the\n        Convention and related conventions to ensure a whole-of-government approach.\n        5.    The national focal points may establish a national platform or use existing national\n        coordination mechanisms, or both, to aid project planning, as necessary, and track ongoing\n        biodiversity funding needs, gaps and priorities. Close links should be established between the\n\n\n19 Decision 15/11, annex.\n20 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619.\n21 Ibid., vol. 3008, No. 30619\n\n\n\n                                                                                                           9/14","blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日</p>"},{"md":"(e) 透過國家報告向締約方大會所通報之資訊，以及締約方透過財務報告架構、調查與訪談之其他提交回應所提供之資訊；\n(f) 全球環境基金理事會所同意，用於判定計畫資助資格之政策與指南；\n(g) 與其他與生物多樣性相關之公約，以及由全球環境基金資助之其他多邊環境協議之間的綜效，包括在運作與影響方面之綜效；\n(h) 透過混合金融（blended finance）所動員之額外私人資本，包括透過使用非撥款工具之方式，同時承認部分締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，在該方面動員私人資本時可能面臨的挑戰；\n(i) 政策一致性；\n(j) 其他相關估算，包括實施性別行動計畫（2023–2030）之成本；¹⁹\n(k) 匯率、通貨膨脹，以及在開發中國家實施公約條款之增量成本。","html":"<p>(e) 透過國家報告向締約方大會所通報之資訊，以及締約方透過財務報告架構、調查與訪談之其他提交回應所提供之資訊；<br />\n(f) 全球環境基金理事會所同意，用於判定計畫資助資格之政策與指南；<br />\n(g) 與其他與生物多樣性相關之公約，以及由全球環境基金資助之其他多邊環境協議之間的綜效，包括在運作與影響方面之綜效；<br />\n(h) 透過混合金融（blended finance）所動員之額外私人資本，包括透過使用非撥款工具之方式，同時承認部分締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，在該方面動員私人資本時可能面臨的挑戰；<br />\n(i) 政策一致性；<br />\n(j) 其他相關估算，包括實施性別行動計畫（2023–2030）之成本；¹⁹<br />\n(k) 匯率、通貨膨脹，以及在開發中國家實施公約條款之增量成本。</p>"},{"md":"3.\n在評估脈絡下，應根據編製報告之需要，進行訪談、調查、定量與定性分析及諮詢，包括：\n(a) 彙編並分析根據公約第六條，由具備全球環境基金資助資格之締約方及其他相關締約方所編製之國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家生物多樣性財務計畫中所識別之需求，包括特定國家之資源動員策略，並應將增量成本資助視為全球環境基金之基本運作原則；\n(b) 審查締約方根據公約第六條與第二十六條，以及卡塔赫納生物安全議定書²⁰第三十三條與名古屋議定書²¹第二十九條所提交之報告，以識別與履行其在公約及其議定書下義務相關之資金需求；\n(c) 締約方向財務機制提供指導建議之預估財務影響；\n(d) 彙編並分析具備全球環境基金資助資格之締約方，就履行其在公約及其議定書下義務之資金需求所提供之任何補充資訊。","html":"<p>3.<br />\n在評估脈絡下，應根據編製報告之需要，進行訪談、調查、定量與定性分析及諮詢，包括：<br />\n(a) 彙編並分析根據公約第六條，由具備全球環境基金資助資格之締約方及其他相關締約方所編製之國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家生物多樣性財務計畫中所識別之需求，包括特定國家之資源動員策略，並應將增量成本資助視為全球環境基金之基本運作原則；<br />\n(b) 審查締約方根據公約第六條與第二十六條，以及卡塔赫納生物安全議定書²⁰第三十三條與名古屋議定書²¹第二十九條所提交之報告，以識別與履行其在公約及其議定書下義務相關之資金需求；<br />\n(c) 締約方向財務機制提供指導建議之預估財務影響；<br />\n(d) 彙編並分析具備全球環境基金資助資格之締約方，就履行其在公約及其議定書下義務之資金需求所提供之任何補充資訊。</p>"},{"md":"C. 實施","html":"<p>C. 實施</p>"},{"md":"4.\n公約之國家聯絡點與財務機制之聯絡點應在適當情況下，與相關利害關係人及公約與相關公約下之其他聯絡點合作，共同負責協調國家層級之增量資金需求評估，以確保採取全政府（whole-of-government）之方法。","html":"<p>4.<br />\n公約之國家聯絡點與財務機制之聯絡點應在適當情況下，與相關利害關係人及公約與相關公約下之其他聯絡點合作，共同負責協調國家層級之增量資金需求評估，以確保採取全政府（whole-of-government）之方法。</p>"},{"md":"5.\n國家聯絡點得視需要建立國家平台或利用現有之國家協調機制，或兩者兼具，以協助計畫規劃，並追蹤進行中之生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項。應在下列各項之間建立密切聯繫：","html":"<p>5.<br />\n國家聯絡點得視需要建立國家平台或利用現有之國家協調機制，或兩者兼具，以協助計畫規劃，並追蹤進行中之生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項。應在下列各項之間建立密切聯繫：</p>"},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />"},{"md":"¹⁹ 決議 15/11，附件。\n²⁰ 聯合國，《聯合國條約集》，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。\n²¹ 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<p>¹⁹ 決議 15/11，附件。<br />\n²⁰ 聯合國，《聯合國條約集》，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n²¹ 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。</p>"}]},{"p":"p010","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae094e458b9a83bc4d4c2ff/p010.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 3 – 27 October 2026\n\n        national platform or relevant coordination mechanism and national support initiatives of relevant\n        funding providers, in particular the country engagement strategy of the Global Environment Facility.\n        6.    The national platform should also facilitate the participation of indigenous peoples and local\n        communities, women and youth organizations and other relevant stakeholders, taking into account\n        the section C of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework, as appropriate, subject to\n        national legislation.\n        7.     The Executive Secretary should provide the information received from Parties without\n        additional reporting obligations on funding needs through an online platform, subject to the\n        availability of resources, to facilitate the visualization of biodiversity funding needs, gaps and\n        priorities on an ongoing basis.\n        8.     The Executive Secretary should prepare a report on the full assessment, and the report should\n        be submitted for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before\n        the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties, with a view to providing recommendations\n        for consideration by the Conference of the Parties at that meeting.\n        9.    At its eighteenth meeting, the Conference of the Parties will be invited to take note of the\n        estimated amount of funds that are necessary for the implementation of the Convention and its\n        Protocols for the tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund.\n\n        Annex III\n        Terms of reference for the seventh quadrennial review\n        of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism\n        A.     Objectives\n        1.    In accordance with paragraph 3 of Article 21 of the Convention on Biological Diversity22 and\n        building upon the experience of the past six reviews of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism,\n        the Conference of the Parties to the Convention will undertake its seventh review at its eighteenth\n        meeting and take appropriate action to improve the effectiveness of the financial mechanism, as\n        necessary. For that purpose, the following elements will be included in the review:\n               (a) The conformity of the activities of the Global Environment Facility, as the institutional\n        structure operating the financial mechanism, with the guidance of the Conference of the Parties;\n               (b) The effectiveness of the financial mechanism in providing financial resources to enable\n        eligible developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island\n        developing States, and Parties with economies in transition to meet the agreed full incremental costs\n        to them of implementing measures through which they fulfil their obligations under the Convention\n        and its Protocols and that generate global environmental benefits, and benefit from their provisions,\n        taking into account the need for predictability, adequacy, accessibility and timely flow of funds,\n        including the performance of the Global Environment Facility implementing agencies;\n               (c) The efficiency of the financial mechanism in providing financial resources and, in\n        accordance with the guidance of the Conference of the Parties, overseeing, monitoring and evaluating\n        the results of activities financed by its resources, including their social and gender- and equity-related\n        outcomes and impacts, as relevant;\n              (d) The effectiveness of catalysing and enhancing national implementation measures in line\n        with national priorities for achieving global biodiversity goals and targets, including those related to\n        the Convention and its Protocols;\n               (e) The efficiency and effectiveness of the activities funded by the Global Environment\n        Facility and the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund for the implementation of the Convention and\n\n\n22 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.\n\n\n\n10/14","blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日</p>"},{"md":"國家平台或相關協調機制，以及相關出資者之國家支持倡議，特別是全球環境基金之國家參與策略。","html":"<p>國家平台或相關協調機制，以及相關出資者之國家支持倡議，特別是全球環境基金之國家參與策略。</p>"},{"md":"6.\n國家平台亦應在符合國家立法之情況下，並視適當情況考慮《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之 C 節，促進原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織及其他相關利害關係人之參與。","html":"<p>6.<br />\n國家平台亦應在符合國家立法之情況下，並視適當情況考慮《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之 C 節，促進原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織及其他相關利害關係人之參與。</p>"},{"md":"7.\n在資源可用之情況下，執行秘書應透過線上平台提供從締約方收到之資訊，且不增加關於資金需求的額外報告義務，以促進持續性地呈現生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項之視覺化。","html":"<p>7.<br />\n在資源可用之情況下，執行秘書應透過線上平台提供從締約方收到之資訊，且不增加關於資金需求的額外報告義務，以促進持續性地呈現生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項之視覺化。</p>"},{"md":"8.\n執行秘書應準備一份完整評估報告，且該報告應提交予執行附屬機構於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議進行審議，旨在為該次締約方大會提供建議。","html":"<p>8.<br />\n執行秘書應準備一份完整評估報告，且該報告應提交予執行附屬機構於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議進行審議，旨在為該次締約方大會提供建議。</p>"},{"md":"9.\n在第十八次會議期間，將邀請締約方大會注意到，為全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期，實施本公約及其議定書所需之估算資金金額。","html":"<p>9.<br />\n在第十八次會議期間，將邀請締約方大會注意到，為全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期，實施本公約及其議定書所需之估算資金金額。</p>"},{"md":"附件 III\n財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之職權範圍","html":"<p>附件 III<br />\n財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之職權範圍</p>"},{"md":"A.\n目標","html":"<p>A.<br />\n目標</p>"},{"md":"1.\n根據《生物多樣性公約》第 21 條第 3 項$^{22}$並基於過去六次財務機制有效性審查之經驗，本公約締約方大會將於其第十八次會議進行第七次審查，並於必要時採取適當行動以提高財務機制之有效性。為此，審查將包含下列要素：\n(a) 作為運作財務機制之制度結構，全球環境基金之活動是否符合締約方大會之指導；\n(b) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面之有效性，以使符合條件之開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中之締約方，能夠承擔其透過實施措施以履行其在本公約及其議定書下之義務，且該等措施能產生全球環境效益並從其規定中獲益之所約定之完整增量成本，並考慮到資金之可預測性、充足性、可取得性與及時流動之需求，包括全球環境基金執行機構之績效；\n(c) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面之效率，並根據締約方大會之指導，對其資源所資助之活動結果進行監督、監測與評估，包括其相關之社會、性別與公平相關之成果與影響；\n(d) 配合達成全球生物多樣性目標與指標之國家優先事項（包括與本公約及其議定書相關之目標），在催化與強化國家實施措施方面之有效性；\n(e) 由全球環境基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助，用於實施本公約之活動之效率與有效性。","html":"<p>1.<br />\n根據《生物多樣性公約》第 21 條第 3 項<sup>22</sup>並基於過去六次財務機制有效性審查之經驗，本公約締約方大會將於其第十八次會議進行第七次審查，並於必要時採取適當行動以提高財務機制之有效性。為此，審查將包含下列要素：<br />\n(a) 作為運作財務機制之制度結構，全球環境基金之活動是否符合締約方大會之指導；<br />\n(b) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面之有效性，以使符合條件之開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中之締約方，能夠承擔其透過實施措施以履行其在本公約及其議定書下之義務，且該等措施能產生全球環境效益並從其規定中獲益之所約定之完整增量成本，並考慮到資金之可預測性、充足性、可取得性與及時流動之需求，包括全球環境基金執行機構之績效；<br />\n(c) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面之效率，並根據締約方大會之指導，對其資源所資助之活動結果進行監督、監測與評估，包括其相關之社會、性別與公平相關之成果與影響；<br />\n(d) 配合達成全球生物多樣性目標與指標之國家優先事項（包括與本公約及其議定書相關之目標），在催化與強化國家實施措施方面之有效性；<br />\n(e) 由全球環境基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助，用於實施本公約之活動之效率與有效性。</p>"},{"md":"---\n$^{22}$ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>22</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。</p>"}]},{"p":"p011","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae094e458b9a83bc4d4c2ff/p011.md","en":"                                                              Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 3 – 27 October 2026\n\n       the achievement of its three objectives, as well as, as applicable, the implementation of its Protocols,\n       taking into account the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties;\n              (f)   The efficiency and effectiveness of processes and procedures for the deployment and\n       use of resources, including simplified procedures and access modalities;\n             (g) The effectiveness and efficiency of the support provided for the objectives of the\n       Convention and its Protocols in synergy with the implementation of other relevant multilateral\n       environmental agreements, in a manner that is consistent with the mandates of the respective\n       agreements;\n             (h) The effectiveness in improving access to financial resources and trends associated with\n       funding for indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth to support the\n       implementation of the objectives of the Convention and its Protocols;\n             (i)    The efficiency of each of the implementing agencies of the Global Environment Facility\n       in providing technical support and services to countries in their preparation of project proposals and\n       the implementation of projects, including with regard to the timely disbursement of fund, fees and\n       project management costs, use of international consultants and control of expenditure.\n       B.     Methodology\n       2.   The review will cover all the activities of the institutional structure operating the financial\n       mechanism, in particular for the period from 1 July 2022 to 30 June 2026.\n       3.    The review shall draw upon, inter alia, and in a balanced manner, the following sources of\n       information:\n             (a) The reviews of effectiveness of the financial mechanism in implementing the\n       Convention undertaken pursuant to the memorandum of understanding between the Conference of\n       the Parties to the Convention and the Council of the Global Environment Facility, as contained in the\n       annex to decision III/8 of 15 November 1996;\n              (b) Reports prepared by the Global Environment Facility, including its reports for meetings\n       of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention;\n              (c) Reports of the Independent Evaluation Office of the Global Environment Facility that\n       relate to the biodiversity-related activities of the Facility, including the eighth comprehensive\n       evaluation of the Global Environment Facility, as well as relevant assessments by the agencies\n       accredited by the Council of the Facility and other partners;\n             [(d) The Multilateral [Organization] Performance [Assessment] Network assessments of the\n       Global Environment Facility [and [relevant] reports] [such as] [related to] the review of the vertical\n       climate and environmental funds under the Group of 20];23]\n             [(d)Alt1    The Multilateral Organization Performance Assessment of the Global\n       Environment Facility and relevant reports of the review of the environmental funds;]\n             (e) Information regarding the financial mechanism provided by Parties through national\n       reports and other submissions, surveys and interviews;\n              (f)   Information provided by indigenous peoples and local communities, women, youth and\n       relevant stakeholders related to projects funded through the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund\n       and the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund, including their views on possible impacts on their\n       rights, as applicable, as well as documented evidence and assessments of such impacts, including\n       gender-differentiated impacts;\n              (g)    Experience with, and lessons learned from, relevant international financial mechanisms;\n\n\n23 See www.mopan.org/en/our-work/performance-evidence/gef.html.\n\n\n\n                                                                                                             11/14","blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日</p>"},{"md":"其三項目標之達成，以及（在適用情況下）其議定書之履行，並考慮締約方大會所提供的指引；\n(f) 資源部署與使用之程序與流程的效率與效能，包括簡化程序與取得模式；\n(g) 在與其他相關多邊環境協議之履行產生綜效，且與各自協議之授權一致之情況下，為公約及其議定書目標所提供之支持的效能與效率；\n(h) 改善取得財務資源之效能，以及與支持原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年以履行公約及其議定書目標相關之資金趨勢；\n(i) 全球環境基金各執行機構在為各國編制計畫提案及執行計畫時，提供技術支援與服務之效率，包括有關資金、費用及計畫管理成本之及時撥付、國際顧問之使用以及支出之控制。","html":"<p>其三項目標之達成，以及（在適用情況下）其議定書之履行，並考慮締約方大會所提供的指引；<br />\n(f) 資源部署與使用之程序與流程的效率與效能，包括簡化程序與取得模式；<br />\n(g) 在與其他相關多邊環境協議之履行產生綜效，且與各自協議之授權一致之情況下，為公約及其議定書目標所提供之支持的效能與效率；<br />\n(h) 改善取得財務資源之效能，以及與支持原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年以履行公約及其議定書目標相關之資金趨勢；<br />\n(i) 全球環境基金各執行機構在為各國編制計畫提案及執行計畫時，提供技術支援與服務之效率，包括有關資金、費用及計畫管理成本之及時撥付、國際顧問之使用以及支出之控制。</p>"},{"md":"B. 方法論","html":"<p>B. 方法論</p>"},{"md":"2.\n本次審查將涵蓋執行財務機制之制度結構的所有活動，特別是自 2022 年 7 月 1 日至 2026 年 6 月 30 日期間。","html":"<p>2.<br />\n本次審查將涵蓋執行財務機制之制度結構的所有活動，特別是自 2022 年 7 月 1 日至 2026 年 6 月 30 日期間。</p>"},{"md":"3.\n審查應以平衡方式，除其他外，利用下列資訊來源：\n(a) 根據 1996 年 11 月 15 日決議 III/8 附件所載，依據本公約締約方大會與全球環境基金理事會間之合作備忘錄所進行之財務機制在履行公約方面之效能審查；\n(b) 由全球環境基金編製之報告，包括其為本公約締約方大會會議所編製之報告；\n(c) 全球環境基金獨立評估辦公室與該基金生物多樣性相關活動有關之報告，包括全球環境基金第八次全面評估，以及由該基金理事會認可之機構及其他合作夥伴所進行之相關評估；\n[(d) 多邊[組織]績效[評估]網絡對全球環境基金之評估[以及[相關]報告][例如][與]二十國集團（G20）架構下垂直氣候與環境基金審查相關之報告]；23]\n[(d) 替代方案 1\n全球環境基金之多邊組織績效評估，以及環境基金審查之相關報告；]\n(e) 締約方透過國家報告及其他提交文件、調查與訪談所提供關於財務機制之資訊；\n(f) 由原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及相關利害關係人所提供，與透過全球環境基金信託基金及全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助之計畫相關之資訊，包括（在適用情況下）其對其權利可能產生影響之看法，以及此類影響（包括性別差異化影響）之文件證據與評估；\n(g) 相關國際財務機制之經驗與經驗教訓；","html":"<p>3.<br />\n審查應以平衡方式，除其他外，利用下列資訊來源：<br />\n(a) 根據 1996 年 11 月 15 日決議 III/8 附件所載，依據本公約締約方大會與全球環境基金理事會間之合作備忘錄所進行之財務機制在履行公約方面之效能審查；<br />\n(b) 由全球環境基金編製之報告，包括其為本公約締約方大會會議所編製之報告；<br />\n(c) 全球環境基金獨立評估辦公室與該基金生物多樣性相關活動有關之報告，包括全球環境基金第八次全面評估，以及由該基金理事會認可之機構及其他合作夥伴所進行之相關評估；<br />\n[(d) 多邊[組織]績效[評估]網絡對全球環境基金之評估[以及[相關]報告][例如][與]二十國集團（G20）架構下垂直氣候與環境基金審查相關之報告]；23]<br />\n[(d) 替代方案 1<br />\n全球環境基金之多邊組織績效評估，以及環境基金審查之相關報告；]<br />\n(e) 締約方透過國家報告及其他提交文件、調查與訪談所提供關於財務機制之資訊；<br />\n(f) 由原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及相關利害關係人所提供，與透過全球環境基金信託基金及全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助之計畫相關之資訊，包括（在適用情況下）其對其權利可能產生影響之看法，以及此類影響（包括性別差異化影響）之文件證據與評估；<br />\n(g) 相關國際財務機制之經驗與經驗教訓；</p>"},{"md":"23 參閱 www.mopan.org/en/our-work/performance-evidence/gef.html。","html":"<p>23 參閱 www.mopan.org/en/our-work/performance-evidence/gef.html。</p>"}]},{"p":"p012","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae094e458b9a83bc4d4c2ff/p012.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 3 – 27 October 2026\n\n              (h) The report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility for the seventeenth\n        meeting of the Conference of the Parties;\n               (i)   The stocktake review of the operations and performance of the Global Biodiversity\n        Framework Fund regarding its scale, speed and accessibility and the future arrangements requested\n        in decision 15/15 of 19 December 2022.\n        C.     Criteria\n        4.           The effectiveness and efficiency of the financial mechanism should be assessed taking\n        into account, inter alia:\n               (a) The actions taken by the Global Environment Facility in response to the guidance of the\n        Conference of the Parties and to the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework,24 including\n        through the decisions of the Global Environment Facility Council on relations with conventions and\n        international institutions;\n                (b) The extent to which [all] eligible Parties[, including developing countries, in particular\n        the least developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in\n        transition] take measures to apply for and receive timely, adequate and predictable funding to enable\n        them to meet the agreed full incremental cost to them of implementing measures through which they\n        fulfil their obligations under the Convention and its Protocols and that generate global environmental\n        benefits;\n               (c) Information provided by Parties in relation to their performance in delivering projects, such\n        as constraints affecting those Parties, as well as women and youth, in delivering those projects, under\n        the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund and the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund, and on\n        the performance of implementing agencies;\n             (d) Percentage of eligible Parties that have received financial support from the financial\n        mechanism for implementing global biodiversity goals and targets, including those related to the\n        Convention and its Protocols;\n               (e) Percentage of biodiversity-relevant funding through the financial mechanism in support\n        of the achievement of global biodiversity goals and targets;\n               (f)   Trends in co-financing, in particular private and non-grant financing in the biodiversity\n        focal area enabled by the financial mechanism;\n              (g) Trends in financing global, regional and subregional biodiversity projects under the\n        financial mechanism;\n              (h) Trends in financing that take into consideration synergies among conventions for which\n        the Global Environment Facility has been designated to operate their financial mechanism on an\n        ongoing and interim basis;\n               (i)   Trends in financing targeted at biodiversity-related conventions and agreements taking\n        into consideration synergies among them;\n              (j) Trends in time frames for project development and resource disbursement, including the\n        time between the approval and the first disbursement;\n              [(k) Trends in financing targeted at or led by indigenous peoples and local communities,\n        women and youth and that respect, protect and fulfil human rights, [including] [and in] [direct]\n        access[25] to finance;]\n\n24 Decision 15/4, annex.\n\n[25 Direct access for organizations of indigenous peoples and local communities include application of procedures for screening\nthe capacities, experience and performance of organizations in managing funds and implementing projects, according to\nestablished Global Environment Facility procedures and following approval by the operational focal points of the Global\nEnvironment Facility, which is granted in coordination with the national focal point for the Convention.]\n\n12/14","blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 版本 3 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 版本 3 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日</p>"},{"md":"(h) 全球環境基金理事會於第十七次締約方大會之報告；\n(i) 針對全球生物多樣性綱要基金之規模、速度與可取得性，以及 2022 年 12 月 19 日決議 15/15 所要求之未來安排，進行其運作與績效之盤點審查。","html":"<p>(h) 全球環境基金理事會於第十七次締約方大會之報告；<br />\n(i) 針對全球生物多樣性綱要基金之規模、速度與可取得性，以及 2022 年 12 月 19 日決議 15/15 所要求之未來安排，進行其運作與績效之盤點審查。</p>"},{"md":"C.","html":"<p>C.</p>"},{"md":"標準","html":"<p>標準</p>"},{"md":"4.\n財務機制之有效性與效率應在考量下列事項時進行評估，其中包括：\n(a) 全球環境基金因應締約方大會之指引及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》$^{24}$ 所採取之行動，包括透過全球環境基金理事會關於與各公約及國際機構關係之決議；\n(b) [所有] 合格締約方[，包括開發中國家，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中之締約方]採取措施申請並獲得及時、充足且可預測之資金之程度，以使其能夠負擔其履行《公約》及其議定書義務，且能產生全球環境效益之措施，其所產生的約定全額增量成本；\n(c) 締約方就其於全球環境基金信託基金及全球生物多樣性綱要基金下執行專案之績效所提供之資訊，例如影響該等締約方、以及女性與青年執行該等專案之限制，以及執行機構之績效；\n(d) 合格締約方中，已透過財務機制獲得財務支持以執行全球生物多樣性目標與指標（包括與《公約》及其議定書相關之目標與指標）之百分比；\n(e) 透過財務機制，用於支持達成全球生物多樣性目標與指標中，與生物多樣性相關之資金百分比；\n(f) 共同融資之趨勢，特別是透過財務機制在生物多樣性重點領域所促成之私人及非撥款型融資趨勢；\n(g) 在財務機制下，資助全球、區域及次區域生物多樣性專案之趨勢；\n(h) 考量到全球環境基金已被指定以持續及臨時方式運作其財務機制之各公約間綜效，其資助之趨勢；\n(i) 考量到各生物多樣性相關公約與協議間綜效，其針對該等公約與協議之資助趨勢；\n(j) 專案開發與資源撥付時程之趨勢，包括從核准至首次撥付之間的時間；\n[(k) 針對原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，且尊重、保護並履行人權之資助趨勢，[包括] [且在] [直接] 取得[$^{25}$]資金之趨勢；]","html":"<p>4.<br />\n財務機制之有效性與效率應在考量下列事項時進行評估，其中包括：<br />\n(a) 全球環境基金因應締約方大會之指引及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》<sup>24</sup> 所採取之行動，包括透過全球環境基金理事會關於與各公約及國際機構關係之決議；<br />\n(b) [所有] 合格締約方[，包括開發中國家，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中之締約方]採取措施申請並獲得及時、充足且可預測之資金之程度，以使其能夠負擔其履行《公約》及其議定書義務，且能產生全球環境效益之措施，其所產生的約定全額增量成本；<br />\n(c) 締約方就其於全球環境基金信託基金及全球生物多樣性綱要基金下執行專案之績效所提供之資訊，例如影響該等締約方、以及女性與青年執行該等專案之限制，以及執行機構之績效；<br />\n(d) 合格締約方中，已透過財務機制獲得財務支持以執行全球生物多樣性目標與指標（包括與《公約》及其議定書相關之目標與指標）之百分比；<br />\n(e) 透過財務機制，用於支持達成全球生物多樣性目標與指標中，與生物多樣性相關之資金百分比；<br />\n(f) 共同融資之趨勢，特別是透過財務機制在生物多樣性重點領域所促成之私人及非撥款型融資趨勢；<br />\n(g) 在財務機制下，資助全球、區域及次區域生物多樣性專案之趨勢；<br />\n(h) 考量到全球環境基金已被指定以持續及臨時方式運作其財務機制之各公約間綜效，其資助之趨勢；<br />\n(i) 考量到各生物多樣性相關公約與協議間綜效，其針對該等公約與協議之資助趨勢；<br />\n(j) 專案開發與資源撥付時程之趨勢，包括從核准至首次撥付之間的時間；<br />\n[(k) 針對原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，且尊重、保護並履行人權之資助趨勢，[包括] [且在] [直接] 取得[<sup>25</sup>]資金之趨勢；]</p>"},{"md":"$^{24}$ 決議 15/4，附件。","html":"<p><sup>24</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。</p>"},{"md":"[$^{25}$ 原住民族與地方社區組織之直接取得，包括根據既定之全球環境基金程序，並經全球環境基金執行焦點聯繫點核准（此核准係與《公約》國家焦點聯繫點協調進行），對組織管理資金與執行專案之能力、經驗與績效進行篩選之程序之應用。]","html":"<p>[<sup>25</sup> 原住民族與地方社區組織之直接取得，包括根據既定之全球環境基金程序，並經全球環境基金執行焦點聯繫點核准（此核准係與《公約》國家焦點聯繫點協調進行），對組織管理資金與執行專案之能力、經驗與績效進行篩選之程序之應用。]</p>"}]},{"p":"p013","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae094e458b9a83bc4d4c2ff/p013.md","en":"                                                   Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 3 – 27 October 2026\n\n      (k) Trends in financing targeted at or led by indigenous peoples and local communities, women\nand youth, including progress on modalities of access to finance;\n      [(l) Trends in the number and themes of capacity-building activities that enable Parties and\nstakeholders to secure access to financing from the Global Environment Facility;]\n       [(m) Trends in project financing leading to high sustainability or durability ratings and long-\nterm results achieved through biodiversity programming supported by the Global Environment\nFacility in relation to expected results planned by the Facility through that programming;]\n      [(n)   Criteria listed in decision 16/34 of 27 February 2025.]\n[5. The assessment should include a comparison of the Global Environment Facility with the\nfinancial mechanisms of other relevant multilateral environmental agreements, including the Green\nClimate Fund[,][ and] the Adaptation Fund [and the Fund for Responding to Loss and Damage].\nElements for consideration should include: contributor base; funding modalities and financial\nperformance; criteria and processes for funding, including project cycle considerations; access and\ndisbursement modalities (e.g. direct allocation or project-based disbursement), including for\nindigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth; relationship between the governing\nbody of the fund and the Conference of the Parties to the respective multilateral environmental\nagreement; transparency, monitoring, reporting and evaluation; accreditation process and role and\nperformance of implementing agencies; cost-effectiveness of operations; ability to leverage funding\nto mobilize additional finance for biodiversity; cost of setting up and running the financial\ninstrument; leveraging public and private co-finance; and integration of various environmental\nfields.]\nD.    Procedures for implementation\n[6. In consultation with the Bureau, the Executive Secretary will contract an experienced\nindependent evaluator to undertake the review, in accordance with the aforementioned objectives,\nmethodology and criteria.]\n[7. The evaluator will undertake desk studies, questionnaire surveys, interviews and field visits,\nsuch as may be required for the implementation of the review, and collaborate for that purpose with\nthe Global Environment Facility and its Independent Evaluation Office, as well as other independent\nassessments, such as those of the Multilateral Performance Network, if necessary, and prepare a\ncompilation and synthesis of the information received.]\n[8. Special efforts should be made to collect the views of Parties, the private sector, indigenous\npeoples and local communities, women and youth, including[, as applicable,] information on possible\nimpacts on their rights [in relation to project-specific environmental objectives and in accordance\nwith relevant national legislation].]\n[9. The draft synthesis report and recommendations of the evaluator will be made available to the\nGlobal Environment Facility for its review and comments. Such comments will be included in the\ndocumentation and identified by source.]\n[10. The report should include as an annex the study requested in paragraph 41 of decision 16/33\nof 27 February 2025 benchmarking the Global Environment Facility against the financial\nmechanisms or similar instruments of other relevant multilateral environmental agreements,\nincluding with regard to their legal nature, funding modalities and financial performance, criteria and\nprocess for funding, access and disbursement modalities, monitoring and evaluation, governance and\nthe cost-effectiveness of operations[, as well as other criteria contained in decision 16/34].]\n10 bis.      The report shall include as an annex the stocktake review referred to in decision 15/15.\n[11. On the basis of the synthesis report and recommendations of the independent evaluator, the\nExecutive Secretary will prepare, in consultation with the Global Environment Facility, a draft\ndecision on the seventh quadrennial review of the financial mechanism, including specific\n\n                                                                                                  13/14","blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日</p>"},{"md":"(k) 針對或由原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年所領導之融資趨勢，包括取得融資方式之進展；\n[(l) 使締約方與利害關係人能夠從全球環境基金取得融資之能力建構活動，其數量與主題之趨勢；]\n[(m) 導致高永續性或高耐久性評級之專案融資趨勢，以及透過全球環境基金支持之生物多樣性計畫所達成之長期成果，與該基金透過該計畫所預期成果之關係；]\n[(n)\n決議 16/34（2025 年 2 月 27 日）所列之標準。]","html":"<p>(k) 針對或由原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年所領導之融資趨勢，包括取得融資方式之進展；<br />\n[(l) 使締約方與利害關係人能夠從全球環境基金取得融資之能力建構活動，其數量與主題之趨勢；]<br />\n[(m) 導致高永續性或高耐久性評級之專案融資趨勢，以及透過全球環境基金支持之生物多樣性計畫所達成之長期成果，與該基金透過該計畫所預期成果之關係；]<br />\n[(n)<br />\n決議 16/34（2025 年 2 月 27 日）所列之標準。]</p>"},{"md":"[5. 評估應包括全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議財務機制之比較，包括綠色氣候基金[,][ 及] 適應基金 [以及應對損失與損害基金]。應考慮之要素應包括：出資者基礎；資助方式與財務績效；資助之標準與程序，包括專案週期之考量；取得與撥付方式（例如：直接分配或以專案為基礎之撥付），包括針對原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年之方式；基金管理機構與各自多邊環境協議締約方大會之間之關係；透明度、監測、報告與評估；認證程序以及執行機構之角色與績效；營運之成本效益；利用資金槓桿以為生物多樣性動員額外資金之能力；建立與運行該財務工具之成本；利用公共與私人共同融資；以及各種環境領域之整合。]","html":"<p>[5. 評估應包括全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議財務機制之比較，包括綠色氣候基金[,][ 及] 適應基金 [以及應對損失與損害基金]。應考慮之要素應包括：出資者基礎；資助方式與財務績效；資助之標準與程序，包括專案週期之考量；取得與撥付方式（例如：直接分配或以專案為基礎之撥付），包括針對原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年之方式；基金管理機構與各自多邊環境協議締約方大會之間之關係；透明度、監測、報告與評估；認證程序以及執行機構之角色與績效；營運之成本效益；利用資金槓桿以為生物多樣性動員額外資金之能力；建立與運行該財務工具之成本；利用公共與私人共同融資；以及各種環境領域之整合。]</p>"},{"md":"D. 執行程序","html":"<p>D. 執行程序</p>"},{"md":"[6. 執行秘書應在諮詢主席團後，聘請一名經驗豐富的獨立評估人員，根據前述目標、方法與標準進行審查。]\n[7. 評估人員應進行書面研究、問卷調查、訪談與實地考察（視執行審查之需要而定），並為此目的與全球環境基金及其獨立評估辦公室進行合作，必要時亦應與其他獨立評估機構（例如多邊績效網絡）進行合作，並編製所收資訊之彙編與綜合報告。]\n[8. 應特別努力收集締約方、私部門、原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年的意見，包括[, 如適用,] 關於對其權利可能產生影響之資訊 [與專案特定環境目標相關，且符合相關國家立法]。]\n[9. 評估人員之綜合報告草案與建議將提交全球環境基金進行審閱與評論。此類評論應納入文件中，並標明來源。]\n[10. 報告應包含一份附件，即決議 16/33（2025 年 2 月 27 日）第 41 段所要求之研究，該研究將全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議之財務機制或類似工具進行基準比較，包括其法律性質、資助方式與財務績效、資助之標準與程序、取得與撥付方式、監測與評估、治理以及營運之成本效益[, 以及決議 16/34 中包含之其他標準]。]","html":"<p>[6. 執行秘書應在諮詢主席團後，聘請一名經驗豐富的獨立評估人員，根據前述目標、方法與標準進行審查。]<br />\n[7. 評估人員應進行書面研究、問卷調查、訪談與實地考察（視執行審查之需要而定），並為此目的與全球環境基金及其獨立評估辦公室進行合作，必要時亦應與其他獨立評估機構（例如多邊績效網絡）進行合作，並編製所收資訊之彙編與綜合報告。]<br />\n[8. 應特別努力收集締約方、私部門、原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年的意見，包括[, 如適用,] 關於對其權利可能產生影響之資訊 [與專案特定環境目標相關，且符合相關國家立法]。]<br />\n[9. 評估人員之綜合報告草案與建議將提交全球環境基金進行審閱與評論。此類評論應納入文件中，並標明來源。]<br />\n[10. 報告應包含一份附件，即決議 16/33（2025 年 2 月 27 日）第 41 段所要求之研究，該研究將全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議之財務機制或類似工具進行基準比較，包括其法律性質、資助方式與財務績效、資助之標準與程序、取得與撥付方式、監測與評估、治理以及營運之成本效益[, 以及決議 16/34 中包含之其他標準]。]</p>"},{"md":"10 bis.","html":"<p>10 bis.</p>"},{"md":"報告應包含一份附件，即決議 15/15 中所述之盤點審查。","html":"<p>報告應包含一份附件，即決議 15/15 中所述之盤點審查。</p>"},{"md":"[11. 執行秘書應根據獨立評估人員之綜合報告與建議，並在諮詢全球環境基金後，準備一份關於財務機制第七次四年一度審查之決議草案，包括特定","html":"<p>[11. 執行秘書應根據獨立評估人員之綜合報告與建議，並在諮詢全球環境基金後，準備一份關於財務機制第七次四年一度審查之決議草案，包括特定</p>"}]},{"p":"p014","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae094e458b9a83bc4d4c2ff/p014.md","en":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – version 3 – 27 October 2026\n\n        suggestions for action to improve the effectiveness of the mechanism[, if necessary,] for\n        consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation, with its recommendations to be submitted\n        to the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting.]\n                                                    __________\n\n\n\n\n14/14","blocks":[{"md":"關於議程第 8 (b) 項之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日","html":"<p>關於議程第 8 (b) 項之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 27 日</p>"},{"md":"旨在提升該機制有效性之行動建議[, 如有必要,]，供執行附屬機構審議，並將其建議提交至第十八次締約方大會。]","html":"<p>旨在提升該機制有效性之行動建議[, 如有必要,]，供執行附屬機構審議，並將其建議提交至第十八次締約方大會。]</p>"}]}]};
